{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success","id":1486924,"title":"Bloodhunt is apparently 5th Edition's biggest success","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-18T17:20:04-07:00","id":1486924,"title":"Bloodhunt is apparently 5th Edition's biggest success","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamepressure.com/newsroom/bloodhunt-with-unexpected-success-on-steam/z4437f\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.gracza.pl/i_gp/h/22/389177233.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamepressure.com/newsroom/bloodhunt-with-unexpected-success-on-steam/z4437f\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloodhunt With Unexpected Success on Steam - gamepressure.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamepressure.com/newsroom/bloodhunt-with-unexpected-success-on-steam/z4437f\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.gamepressure.com/newsroom/bloodhunt-with-unexpected-success-on-steam/z4437f </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The debut of version 1.0 of Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodhunt turned out to be a great success. The game achieves impressive activity results and receives good reviews from users. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.videogameschronicle.com/features/interviews/vampire-bloodhunt-interview-no-one-wants-to-work-on-a-pay-to-win-game/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.videogameschronicle.com/files/2022/04/ss_d7d120237c38ce0cfd88227b0e371f436cc09d91.1920x1080.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.videogameschronicle.com/features/interviews/vampire-bloodhunt-interview-no-one-wants-to-work-on-a-pay-to-win-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire Bloodhunt Interview: &lsquo;No one wants to work on a pay-to-win game&rsquo; | VGC </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.videogameschronicle.com/features/interviews/vampire-bloodhunt-interview-no-one-wants-to-work-on-a-pay-to-win-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.videogameschronicle.com/features/interviews/vampire-bloodhunt-interview-no-one-wants-to-work-on-a-pay-to-win-game/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sharkmob's director and producer discuss the future of their stylish and brutal PS5 and PC battle royale&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://toptwitchstreamers.com/bloodhunt-devs-success/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://toptwitchstreamers.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Bloodhunt-Devs-On-Its-Success.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://toptwitchstreamers.com/bloodhunt-devs-success/\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloodhunt Devs Success </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://toptwitchstreamers.com/bloodhunt-devs-success/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://toptwitchstreamers.com/bloodhunt-devs-success/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bloodhunt, Sharkmob's Vampire: The Masquerade-inspired battle royale, has captivated Twitch behemoths like Shroud, and iiTzTimmy, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodhunt-future-interview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/bloodhunt_future_header.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;enable=upscale&amp;auto=webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodhunt-future-interview\" target=\"_blank\"> More story, more communication, more content &ndash; how Sharkmob plans to support Bloodhunt for years to come </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodhunt-future-interview\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.vg247.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodhunt-future-interview </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> We sit down with David Sirland, producer on Vampire Bloodhunt, to talk about the games' future, live service updates and more. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, I have to admit I did not see this coming but probably should have. Fifth Edition has had some serious issues with its spin off material and the present vaporware of Bloodlines was the biggest sorrow of the product. I really had hope for Swansong but it seems like the money-making success that Paradox Interactive wanted from buying the World of Darkness has been achieved in their battle royale game.<br /> <br /> It's not a Fortnite killer, hell no, but it IS a success and seems to be set for money to continue pouring in for the time being.<br /> <br /> It is the Mandalorian of their Disney purchase of Star Wars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T17:34:16-07:00","id":1486926,"title":"","content":"Only the Malk story in Swansong is compelling, and the voice acting and animation is terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T19:40:27-07:00","id":1486935,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth considering that, esp. in the f2p battle royale genre, getting a good reception is not the same as being successful. While something players love, a purely cosmetics based monetization system needs a pretty big audience to have money &quot;pouring in,&quot; no matter how much players like it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you need a giant audience to make this profitable if cosmetics are really going to be the only money maker here. If, on average, Bloodhunt makes $10 per registered player per month... that's barely enough to support the dozens of full time employees which is a minimum of what it takes to run this sort of game at their current numbers. There's a huge risk at the moment of Bloodhunt not growing fast enough to sustain itself, or changes in monetization necessary become sustainable that alienates new customers and leaves a stagnant player base.<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt is absolutely having a great start. It needs to have a great next year or two before we know if this is really a success on a corporate level. There are lots of great games/movies/etc. that are really well liked, but bomb financially because they don't generate sales to remake production (and Bloodhunt could not have been cheap to make).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:07:24-07:00","id":1486938,"title":"","content":"I can't get any wins in bloodhunt. I am 99.99% sure that for every 1 hour I have played the game, my opponents have played 100. Tell me I'm not the only one dealing with this.<br /> <br /> It's a great game, but it feels downright impossible to win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-18-2022, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:49:05-07:00","id":1486948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486935#post1486935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth considering that, esp. in the f2p battle royale genre, getting a good reception is not the same as being successful. While something players love, a purely cosmetics based monetization system needs a pretty big audience to have money &quot;pouring in,&quot; no matter how much players like it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you need a giant audience to make this profitable if cosmetics are really going to be the only money maker here. If, on average, Bloodhunt makes $10 per registered player per month... that's barely enough to support the dozens of full time employees which is a minimum of what it takes to run this sort of game at their current numbers. There's a huge risk at the moment of Bloodhunt not growing fast enough to sustain itself, or changes in monetization necessary become sustainable that alienates new customers and leaves a stagnant player base.<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt is absolutely having a great start. It needs to have a great next year or two before we know if this is really a success on a corporate level. There are lots of great games/movies/etc. that are really well liked, but bomb financially because they don't generate sales to remake production (and Bloodhunt could not have been cheap to make).</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually have the Steam data for Bloodhunt so it's not the case where we have to debate the questions of success or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://steamcharts.com/app/760160\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://steamcharts.com/assets/steam-images/760160.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://steamcharts.com/app/760160\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodhunt - Steam Charts </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://steamcharts.com/app/760160\" target=\"_blank\"> https://steamcharts.com/app/760160 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> An ongoing analysis of Steam's player numbers, seeing what's been played the most. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/C6YU3SB.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Really, the big thing I've gotten from the articles is the fact that Blood Hunt is visually distinct enough that it has managed to attract a regular group of players and purchasers of cosmetics that the developers themselves have stated is the source of the vast majority of its monetization. We've also got plans to continue to expand the game with new Clans, storytelling mode, and arenas so they've managed to make enough from it that they're continuing forward. I don't play Battle Royale games and I admit I haven't experienced this myself despite the fact that I usually buy everything World of Darkness related.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm happy for the success as it may be because it is the biggest advertising for the IP right now there is and a nice protection against the fact there's nothing else really coming out until Bloodlines 2 and the television shows.<br /> <br /> It's popular enough to get a Honest Game Trailer and that's nothing to sneeze at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MK4dxeEA9NY\" data-code=\"MK4dxeEA9NY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MK4dxeEA9NY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-18-2022, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:16:00-07:00","id":1486954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486938#post1486938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't get any wins in bloodhunt. I am 99.99% sure that for every 1 hour I have played the game, my opponents have played 100. Tell me I'm not the only one dealing with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you're not. \ud83d\ude02 Steam tells me I have clocked in over a 100 hours on <i>Bloodhunt,</i> and I've long since accepted that getting a solo win is a pipe dream for a person with the reflexes of someone in his late thirties. I've had a win here and there in trios, but each time I've felt like I was the least contributing player out of three. It's just the nature of the beast that the top percentage of Battle Royale players are more or less untouchable for scrubs like me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:55:50-07:00","id":1486960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486948#post1486948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We actually have the Steam data for Bloodhunt so it's not the case where we have to debate the questions of success or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's players, not profits.<br /> <br /> Fortnite has 350-400 <b>million </b>unique users. It regularly has 5+ million users playing at any given moment. 29K peak users every is not &quot;money pouring in&quot; numbers in this genre of game.<br /> <br /> All those features Bloodhunt is playing to put out? Every battle royale has years of features planned (that's the whole &quot;roadmap&quot; thing you linked to in one of the articles). Most of those features never happen outside of the biggest money makers in the genre because it takes a combination of profit and good developer management to make that happen.<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt needs to grow, exponentially, to fund the things it wants to do over the next few years. It certainly has the potential to carve out a space to do that, but it's not a financial success at the numbers posted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T22:52:05-07:00","id":1486964,"title":"","content":"It's not really fair to compare Bloodhunt to Fortnite. <br /> <br /> But, that said, assuming an average of around 3000 players per day, and if each player spends $10 per month, that comes out to a grand total of $360,000 a year. If you have 6 people on the development team and they're each earning $60,00 a year (which is not very much in the tech industry), that's the entirely yearly income of the game with nothing left over for servers, hardware or profit. And keep in mind that with a game like this, you need artists and programmers constantly making new skins, animations, etc, so that people <i>can</i> spend $10 a month. <br /> <br /> Ultimately what it comes down to is how much money and how long the company is willing to invest into the game. There are some games that aren't super popular right off the bat, but word of mouth attracts more players and eventually they end up being profitable. Maybe that will be Bloodhunt. But the developer could look at those numbers and say, &quot;Nah, it's not where it needs to be. Investing more money is a waste. Pull the plug,&quot; and it could end up dead before getting large enough to be self-sustaining, and it certainly wouldn't be the first time we've seen something like that happen. <br /> <br /> Of course Bloodhunt was based on a fairly obscure IP (by mainstream standards) and even for people familiar with the IP, it's not the genre you'd usually associate with it. I'm guessing the developer considered that stuff when okaying the game in the first place, so I don't think there's any risk of the game being shut down in the near future, unless the numbers absolutely tank.<br /> <br /> So basically those numbers aren't low enough for me to write the game off as a failure, but they're definitely not high enough for me to be willing to bet on the game's long-term future either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T23:16:35-07:00","id":1486966,"title":"","content":"I think it's probably far more than 3000 players per day given that it is 2000 players at a time and 20K at once and this is all just one month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T00:19:36-07:00","id":1486971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486964#post1486964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really fair to compare Bloodhunt to Fortnite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. But the most popular battle royale in the world makes ~$10-15 per unique player a year. Fortnite grosses billions, but that's because of its scale.<br /> <br /> The point of bringing up Fortnite is that the money in this business model relies on having lots of players, or it's player base to spend way more than what many companies can get players to do.<br /> <br /> As you note, Bloodhunt needs a lot more players that spend average battle royale money, or we need to see that players are tossing a lot of money by industry standards.<br /> <br /> Like I said, Bloodhunt could make a niche for itself in this market. But we don't have the data for that yet. It has all the potential to do so, but potential doesn't always pan out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486966#post1486966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's probably far more than 3000 players per day given that it is 2000 players at a time and 20K at once and this is all just one month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Below the chart you posted an image of, Steam has a table of average players per day per month. May '22 was ~13K average players, June '22 ~2.8K average daily players,and the last 30 days is only averaging ~1.4K players.<br /> <br /> That's actually really bad. While it's always inevitable to see a large month on the first day of full release after beta slows and ends, but a drop off after, those numbers need to start going up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T00:32:38-07:00","id":1486972,"title":"","content":"I dunno, all the articles I linked to are all about how it's a huge success.<br /> <br /> What do you think of them?<br /> <br /> I mean, literally, this is the first headline:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Bloodhunt With Unexpected Success on Steam</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>The debut of version 1.0 of Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodhunt turned out to be a great success. The game achieves impressive activity results and receives good reviews from users.</i></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to SteamCharts, the game\u2019s population is growing at an exponential rate, and Bloodhunt Producer David Sirland has opened up about how it feels to have their game picked up by some of the gaming world\u2019s biggest names. </div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-19-2022, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:01:51-07:00","id":1486976,"title":"","content":"Look at the dates.<br /> <br /> The article you're quoting is from May. In May Bloodhunt posted 13K avg players a day with a peak of 29K users at one moment. Two months later, that's dropped to 1.4K avg players, and 3.3K peak players.<br /> <br /> Just look at Steams data that you yourself linked to: Bloodhunt is doing 1/10 of how good it was in May, and those May numbers were not runaway smash hit numbers by themselves. If things were consistently increasing from May? Bloodhunt would be on the fast track towards smash hit you seem to be reading it is. But the data is currently indicating a flash in the pan is a serious concern for the game. By next May, it needs to either demonstrate an astoundingly high microtransaction rate for the genre, or it needs something closer to 100K to 200K avg players a day, or the money on overhead and keeping a staff employed to constantly roll out new content and features isn't going to be there. <br /> <br /> Let me stress this again. Fortnite makes about ~$13 per average active user per <b>year</b> That is, on average, a player plays less than $2 a month there. And it's the biggest game in the genre. 3K avg players a day being &quot;normal&quot; for Bloodhunt would mean $40K gross (not net, gross) income off the game per year if players spend on it like they do on Fortnite. That's not enough to keep the lights on, let alone pay anyone.<br /> <br /> As Anubis pointed out, even if Bloodhunt players were paying twelve times as much money as Fortnite players, that's still a shoestring budget for a game under this model.<br /> <br /> There needs to be way, way, way more players of this game for it to be a success under this model. And the numbers are currently (if not sky-is-falling doom and gloom of a situation) going in the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> I get you want to find a positive light here, but the numbers are what the numbers are. Bloodhunt, however good of a game it is, might be too ambitious for its own good, because there isn't the money to backup the quality of the game as it currently stands. That's the harsh reality of this genre of video game. It's why so many of these games try to extract way more money out of players even if they avoid pay-to-win.<br /> <br /> Again, think Bloodhunt has the potential to survive this. Everything I've seen says it could be a solid game that finds it's niche and gets up to those higher levels of regular players needed for this type of product to work, because being a good game out of the box means a lot these days. But I can't tell how you can look at the numbers and see sunshine and roses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:15:13-07:00","id":1486977,"title":"","content":"I suppose the issue here is you're comparing it to Fornite, one of the most profitable games of all time, and I'm comparing it to the other WOD licensed games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:27:10-07:00","id":1486978,"title":"","content":"More like the only success so far, all of the spin off material (and most of the books I would add) have been a complete disappointment, I dread to think what they will do with that tv series they were planning to be honest, I still have hopes for bloodlines 2 but the situation doesn't look great...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:39:59-07:00","id":1486979,"title":"","content":"Pretty awkward considering v5 has been tooting it's horn about how it's a deep game about the struggle against the beast while discouraging combat and then they release a battle royale game which does well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:42:43-07:00","id":1486980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486979#post1486979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty awkward considering v5 has been tooting it's horn about how it's a deep game about the struggle against the beast while discouraging combat and then they release a battle royale game which does well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wish you could do in V5 half the things you do in bloodhunt lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T03:54:40-07:00","id":1486981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486977#post1486977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the issue here is you're comparing it to Fornite, one of the most profitable games of all time, and I'm comparing it to the other WOD licensed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm comparing it as far as I am to Fortnite because Fortnite is the same kind of product. Comparing Bloodhunt to different types of games with different economic realities is meaningless. Bloodhunt will probably never make as significant profit compared to Fortnite, but Bloodhunt makes money the same way Fortnite does. Bloodhunt has to be successful the way Fortnite is successful even if on a smaller scale. It can't be successful in some different fashion.<br /> <br /> Like, a huge difference? Most WoD licensed products don't have ongoing overhead of a significant nature. Swansong is done. They made it. Profit off it is selling enough copies. If it was super popular and successful you might have some people doing some quarterly patches or whatnot to ensure long tail sales. Bloodhunt is a constant content driven game. You have to have artists and programmers making new cosmetics for people to buy, or your don't make money on it. There's a minimum bar of money coming in that justifies the game's existence because there are staff to pay, servers to maintain, anti-cheat third parties to send their money, etc. You can't toss a f2p battle royale up on Steam and hope you make more money than it cost to make.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T04:13:32-07:00","id":1486982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486980#post1486980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wish you could do in V5 half the things you do in bloodhunt lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said before theirs nothing wrong with a bit of katanas and trenchcoats even if I don't personally care for it. It is afterall, quite fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-19-2022, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T04:28:12-07:00","id":1486983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486982#post1486982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I've said before theirs nothing wrong with a bit of katanas and trenchcoats even if I don't personally care for it. It is afterall, quite fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have never been a fan of superheroes with fangs myself but I think that V5 focuses way too much on the shittiness of vampire existence without that omf factor that V20 and Requiem had, you just don't feel powerful enough in V5 and the disciplines are extremely situational at best, of course the videogames are going to bump vamps powers, hell even nightroad bumped up vamps in general and it's a novel game basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T04:35:24-07:00","id":1486984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486977#post1486977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the issue here is you're comparing it to Fornite, one of the most profitable games of all time, and I'm comparing it to the other WOD licensed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not comparing it to Fortnite, he's using Fortnite to exemplify the numbers of money pouring in. There are two distinct comparison going on here.<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt is, as far as we can see, the greatest hit among WoD-based games. The best reception and the greatest gross sales to date. People plainly like it more than any of the others, give or take personal taste with game genre.<br /> <br /> Yet the OP isn't just saying that, but also implying <u>success</u>, and that's a far trickier definition. What is success?<br /> <br /> From the perspective of a player of course it is quality and a large fan base to talk with about the game. But from the perspective of the companies involved it is this and a lot of other things in a context whose <i>end result</i> is <b>profit</b>.<br /> <br /> The problem is that profit doesn't depend on comparing with the rest of the IP, it depends on the size and cost of the project itself. As far as we can tell most other VtM games may have got enough net profit to at least make it even, but they're small projects whose costs are concentrated in development itself, then they just have to wait for the money to pour in without expending much more. <b>Bloodhunt</b> is a Battle Royal, it <b>must</b> be taken as a Battle Royal. It had a greater budget to pay off and has to keep servers and ongoing development. It isn't ever a finished product, it'll only stop costing good money when it stops making any money at all.<br /> <br /> So its initial success may be a good sign, but it isn't nearly enough. The game didn't even paid itself as far as we can tell, and it needs to stay afloat on top of that. Every day keeps the cost going up for the profit to play catch up. It <b>needs</b> to gross over a year enough to pay its own basic costs at the very least, which includes at least a couple dedicated developers/staff to handle it.<br /> <br /> Lets not forget: for all the (deserved) cult around it, the original <b>Bloodlines</b> was a blunder, not a hit. It didn't grossed enough to recoup costs before it spelled doom on the devs. And the problem was precisely that it was too ambitious a project for the time, team and budget they had. It cost a lot, took too long, ended up being released unfinished because of that and didn't made enough to secure new projects for Troika. <b>And this is our gold standard</b>. Bloodhunt is too big of a project to follow its footsteps, it <b>has</b> to surpass <b>Bloodlines</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T04:46:38-07:00","id":1486985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486983#post1486983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have never been a fan of superheroes with fangs myself but I think that V5 focuses way too much on the shittiness of vampire existence without that omf factor that V20 and Requiem had, you just don't feel powerful enough in V5 and the disciplines are extremely situational at best, of course the videogames are going to bump vamps powers, hell even nightroad bumped up vamps in general and it's a novel game basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vtm has ways had a slight disconnect with its fanbase which has slowly escalated overtime. While I'm weary of using superheroes with fangs(it's closer to sin city than avengers 45-self aware boogaloo) as a descriptor theirs clearly a strong tendacy to exalt in the vampiric condition, even the new v5 players are doing this in their art. I recall seeing a blood brother via gender queer Harley quinn on vtm reddit and all I could think was how fun that looked All.the while the game constantly emphasises how rotten it is being a vampire and the powers are now pretty mediocre and then they released a battle royal.<br /> <br /> Lol the fuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-19-2022, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T05:15:34-07:00","id":1486987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486985#post1486985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vtm has ways had a slight disconnect with its fanbase which has slowly escalated overtime. While I'm weary of using superheroes with fangs(it's closer to sin city than avengers 45-self aware boogaloo) as a descriptor theirs clearly a strong tendacy to exalt in the vampiric condition, even the new v5 players are doing this in their art. I recall seeing a blood brother via gender queer Harley quinn on vtm reddit and all I could think was how fun that looked All.the while the game constantly emphasises how rotten it is being a vampire and the powers are now pretty mediocre and then they released a battle royal.<br /> <br /> Lol the fuck?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have always been of the opinion that they badly screwed the pooch with V5, mechanics wise is definitely an improvement (although there is still tons of space for balance and tweaking) but thematically they are all over the place, you say kindred are rotten to the core yet you actively penalize players who want to play anything but a goody two shoes high gen neonate, you say that vampires have immesurable powers yet half the disciplines are a joke and the others are extremely situational, you say that kindreds are cunning predators apt to exist amongst the living yet the hunger dices turn vampires into ticking bombs ready to go off at the slightest provocation, jeez fellas make up your mind!<br /> <br /> I won't even go into the metaplot and how ridiculous it is right now, seems like a badly written fan fiction to be honest, even the supposedly &quot;good&quot; supplements like chicago by night are merely so by comparison to the rest of the line, on their own they are merely mediocre especially when compared to the rest of the stuff onyx path made.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant but I'm in the process of making a one shot for V5 and I'm growing more and more frustrated the more I read into the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T05:57:28-07:00","id":1486989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486977#post1486977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the issue here is you're comparing it to Fornite, one of the most profitable games of all time, and I'm comparing it to the other WOD licensed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's a pretty good model to compare to. Fortnite is also a free to play game with premium content being available for playtime and in app purchases. So the model is literally the same, and a game of Fortnite's caliber expects an average spend of 13$ per active player. Even with existance of superfan whales in either playerbase covering for many who never pay a dime but still play, but how many whales would a game with 40 000 active players need to actually eke out a profitable existance?<br /> <br /> And do keep in mind that this model is generous! Thanks to the insane playerbase the profitability of Fortnite is much higher on average than most other F2P products.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:48:23-07:00","id":1486998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486989#post1486989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it's a pretty good model to compare to. Fortnite is also a free to play game with premium content being available for playtime and in app purchases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> It's talking about how much they're getting from the use of the WOD license.<br /> <br /> Quite a few of the game uses so far have utterly failed to make it to market or been disasters ill-received with the public.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486987#post1486987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't even go into the metaplot and how ridiculous it is right now, seems like a badly written fan fiction to be honest, <b>even the supposedly &quot;good&quot; supplements like chicago by night are merely so by comparison to the rest of the line, o</b>n their own they are merely mediocre especially when compared to the rest of the stuff onyx path made.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant but I'm in the process of making a one shot for V5 and I'm growing more and more frustrated the more I read into the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for me, Chicago by Night 1st Edition and 5th Edition are the two greatest supplements for V:TM period.<br /> <br /> BJD is the best after it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-19-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T07:06:09-07:00","id":1487002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486998#post1486998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> It's talking about how much they're getting from the use of the WOD license.<br /> <br /> Quite a few of the game uses so far have utterly failed to make it to market or been disasters ill-received with the public.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that if the numbers don't go up, Bloodhunt will just be the F2P version of a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T07:12:09-07:00","id":1487003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487002#post1487002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that if the numbers don't go up, Bloodhunt will just be the F2P version of a disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the articles are already showing it's by far the most successful release they've done and already a success and it's performing far better than expected so I guess I don't get that angle of discussion.<br /> <br /> I suppose I am thinking about what this means for the brand and franchise as a whole that the combat-heavy no-story game is the one that succeeded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerR