up, Bloodhunt will just be the F2P version of a disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps if you remember that F2P means &quot;we dumped a couple of million dollars into this hoping we will recoup the costs and profit over the period of service&quot;. If the service has low numbers and user spending.... Ooooops.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T08:09:36-07:00","id":1487011,"title":"","content":"I find it a little funny that V5's greatest success has nothing to do with V5, it was just released in the V5 era. But really it just seems a bit beyond VTM; More &quot;inspired by&quot; than &quot;based on&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T11:27:17-07:00","id":1487031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487004#post1487004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It helps if you remember that F2P means &quot;we dumped a couple of million dollars into this hoping we will recoup the costs and profit over the period of service&quot;. If the service has low numbers and user spending.... Ooooops.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's getting articles about how much of a success it was so again I feel like it's weird to say otherwise. It's also a licensed product so Paradox made its bank no matter what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487011#post1487011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it a little funny that V5's greatest success has nothing to do with V5, it was just released in the V5 era. But really it just seems a bit beyond VTM; More &quot;inspired by&quot; than &quot;based on&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>For once I am in total agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-19-2022, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T13:01:06-07:00","id":1487047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1486984#post1486984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodhunt is, as far as we can see, the greatest hit among WoD-based games. The best reception and the greatest gross sales to date. People plainly like it more than any of the others, give or take personal taste with game genre.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say that the old HtR games, however much they have failed to retain cultural relevance, hold this title. So far, HtR had the best video game launch and reception of any WoD product. It came out with strong numbers, had good reviews from both HtR TTRPG fans and twin stick shooter fans (it was largely considered the best twin stick game on the original XBox), was financially profitable and had two sequels that both performed well.<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt is currently behind HtR, even if people tend to forget that the HtR video games existed in these discussions, though CT is more talking the Paradox era so there's that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487003#post1487003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the articles are already showing it's by far the most successful release they've done and already a success and it's performing far better than expected so I guess I don't get that angle of discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because <b>that's not what the articles are showing</b>.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how we can explain this differently. Bloodhunt is <b>not a one-and-done</b> product. It's not something that you claim success on based on how many people get it on release, and then future sales are all gravy. Bloodhunt <b>is a service</b>. It needs a constant flow of customers to be successful. It needs subscribers (even though you &quot;subscribe&quot; via microtransactions), that endure over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose I am thinking about what this means for the brand and franchise as a whole that the combat-heavy no-story game is the one that succeeded. </div> </div> </div>It hasn't succeeded yet. You seem to think that having a great opening month = success. But that's not how f2p games work. Bloodhunt is close to bombing right now because June and July look like they're going to see a 90% decrease in play (and play = success, not downloads).<br /> <br /> You know what, read this, and consider who it's from:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://bloodhunt.com/en-us/news/what-is-going-on-with-bloodhunt-part-one\" target=\"_blank\">https://bloodhunt.com/en-us/news/wha...dhunt-part-one</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The truth is in the numbers</b><br /><br /> Unfortunately, the data shows us that our hourly concurrent players is going down, and that weekends are the moment where we have slightly more people playing, which is the reason we have to make some tough calls while we are getting the next update done. Your sentiment, as positive it was about disabling cross play during the weekend, did not lead to players returning in the scale we were hoping for. Especially not in regions outside of Europe and North America, which means that we simply have to accept that unless players return in these regions, longer matchmaking will have to be a reality for now until the player count increases. Also, we are hearing your criticism of the frequent rotations interfering with your favorite play mode being rotated out. This is something we must address, though we must accept some concessions.<br /> We also hear you that we are too infrequent with our game updates, so we have adjusted our priorities and improved our internal processes to be able to release updates more often, which means more stuff to you, our players. </div> </div> </div>That's from the official Bloodhunt blog from 11 days ago, not some article from over two months ago. Sharkmob is on the fucking ropes. They know their current numbers are garbage and they're praying that the July and August updates turn things around. Think about that official statement from the company that wide released this game less than three months ago. The open acknowledgement that game play is going to suffer because the player base isn't returning.<br /> <br /> You want to talk about what this means for the brand? What does the WoD transmedia brand look like if Bloodhunt dies in September or October because the numbers never recover? Bloodlines 2 is &quot;still in development,&quot; the released videogames are meh, and Bloodhunt bombs horribly. The WoD brand is going to turn toxic to bigger developers because the IP doesn't get sales even with games with good mechanics. Bloodhunt being WoD is - if current trends continue - not enough to get a good battle royale game to break through the rest to find a spot in the genre. WoD will get marked as being a drag to products instead of a boon to them. Why pay Paradox to make WoD branded IF games, or vampire themed Disco Elysium if you can just make those games without the WoD branding and do just as well?<br /> <br /> How the hell can the brand afford Bloodhunt to bomb after a few months?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487031#post1487031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's getting articles about how much of a success it was so again I feel like it's weird to say otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Find us a positive article from July. And it's not weird to say otherwise <u>if you pay attention to how this specific type of game works</u>.<br /> <br /> What you're doing, is treating all of Paradox's big hype campaign around Bloodlines 2 as success, and then ignoring everything that happened afterwords (like us not having a game yet). Because that's all the articles and first month activity is: hype. It's not the product, it's not success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also a licensed product so Paradox made its bank no matter what. </div> </div> </div>In the short term, yes. How many potential future deals are at risk if Bloodlines 2 continues to languish in development hell and Bloodhunt flops?<br /> <br /> If the WoD IP consistently proves to not be worth it for other video game companies to want to pay for the licensing, Paradox's whole business model for the WoD is in trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T14:34:23-07:00","id":1487060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487031#post1487031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's getting articles about how much of a success it was so again I feel like it's weird to say otherwise. It's also a licensed product so Paradox made its bank no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly,no. That doesn't mean that, because that's not how licensing works. If you license something you get certain terms. This tends to be X money up front, and Y money as percentage of sales with a most likely minimum amount of money to be paid out. This lasts a period of time of Z before it's renegotiated. Considering the shotgun approach and varied devs Paradox is farming this out to X is most likely not a very large number, and it's not what makes the license profitable. It's the Y that you want, and Y where the big money is.<br /> <br /> For the developers its even worse because they probably have contractual obligations now, and they still paid X and minimum Y to Paradox. It's a bad deal for them, and while Paradox has more money than if they did nothing, they are poisoning the well by making the license unattractive to other studios. Why bother paying X and Y if you don't even get an IP that guarrantees sales!<br /> <br /> Also, seconding everything Heavy Arms just eloquently said.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T19:41:08-07:00","id":1487091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487047#post1487047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the short term, yes. How many potential future deals are at risk if Bloodlines 2 continues to languish in development hell and Bloodhunt flops?<br /> <br /> If the WoD IP consistently proves to not be worth it for other video game companies to want to pay for the licensing, Paradox's whole business model for the WoD is in trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original <b>Bloodlines</b> flopped, but eventually made it even and today can be considered a success.<br /> <br /> Yet, it <b><u>killed</u></b> Troika Games. Why? Because its flop meant they couldn't get a contract for another project. They went down the following year, not because the game wasn't making <b>any</b> money, but because wasn't making <b>good PR with publishers</b>.<br /> <br /> It is a business. It needs to convince shareholders that they'll get the expected profit from their investment. It needs to convince them this game will give more return than concurrent investments.<br /> <br /> Paradox launched V5 4 years ago, and actually started to ask for pitches on games earlier (I got their form in November 2017 myself, and I was late already). As far as anyone can tell, while the game industry had a peak during the Pandemic, WoD is dragging down. Paradox itself just had its best semester ever, but not thanks to anything WoD-related. They <b>are</b> devs and aren't making any WoD game themselves.<br /> <br /> Currently Paradox is running a project of pre-approved licensing with no strings attached so people can develop games using the IP and not have it as canon, then negotiate canonization if it goes well, similar to the ST Vault. This is interesting, but also seems like a desperate move from the IP perspective in the way it was done. No big name is interested, the IP is yet to show promise, and games continue to not contribute a lot. If this trend isn't reversed by the next releases, then the only thing maintaining the IP will be good will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T20:31:41-07:00","id":1487101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487091#post1487091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently Paradox is running a project of pre-approved licensing with no strings attached so people can develop games using the IP and not have it as canon, then negotiate canonization if it goes well, similar to the ST Vault. This is interesting, but also seems like a desperate move from the IP perspective in the way it was done. No big name is interested, the IP is yet to show promise, and games continue to not contribute a lot. If this trend isn't reversed by the next releases, then the only thing maintaining the IP will be good will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understand this is just my theory but I believe Paradox Interactive is currently doing the majority of things it's doing for the purposes of spreading the IP around. They've signed deals for World of Darkness movies and television shows. They also DO want to make the massively successful (hopefully) Bloodlines 2 and perhaps more games of its like.<br /> <br /> Everything else is really just advertising for these. I think they overestimated how much popularity the 20 year old World of Darkness IP had inside the United States and perhaps outside of it so a lot of what they're doing is based around getting word of mouth out that it alive and well.<br /> <br /> It's why I believe V5 is never going to be amended because the purpose of V5 is to make the most adaptation friendly World of Darkness possible. Which is the following:<br /> <br /> <u><b>V5 as a Story Bible</b></u><br /> <br /> * <b>Anarchs</b>: Good. Scrappy underdog poor kids and street punks.<br /> <br /> * <b>Camarilla</b>: Snooty. Bad. But still sexy and kind of awesome.<br /> <br /> * <b>Sabbat</b>: The scary bad guys you can kill with impunity.<br /> <br /> * <b>Hunters</b>: The government is big, nasty, and scary and out to kill you poor Anarchs when you don't want vampire opponents but just guys with guns. Also, why does the government not intervene? Because they're already hunting you.<br /> <br /> * <b>Clan Changes: </b>Make it all as simplified and straightforward as you need.<br /> <br /> *<b> Continuity Soft Reboot</b>: Only a handful of spinoffs have any reference to older canon.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, I don't think this is a BAD thing necessarily but it could have been handled MUCH-MUCH better and OPP pretty much should have been asked to do it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T21:56:33-07:00","id":1487109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <b>Camarilla</b>: Snooty. Bad. But still sexy and kind of awesome </div> </div> </div>Anything tabletop rpg related not from OPP, and that seems to be basically everything onwards for V5 at this point (unless you've read something I personally missed), has them as more or less incompetent or diabolical (or both) cartoon villains that come with a borderline lecture that selecting this play option makes you bad as a person, or certainly at least one that has bad ideas about gaming. Honestly, other than Chicago by Night itself and its direct spinoffs, where do you get &quot;kind of awesome&quot; from? That's the main OPP book with a major Camarilla focus (and the direct spinoffs it has), the others that exist focus on other things.<br /> <br /> Really even the promotional efforts meant to take advantage of new audiences that come in to ttrpgs via the actual play genre like LA by Night lean pretty heavily into &quot;the Camarilla are basically evil, morons, and evil morons, who you will look good against no matter how bad you are, and your job is to fight them. Look, Matt Mercer's npc is saying the Camarilla is bad, you like Matt Mercer, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Haven't watched New York yet, I tend to wait for these things to finish so I can take them in as a whole)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's the thing, I don't think this is a BAD thing necessarily but it could have been handled MUCH-MUCH better and OPP pretty much should have been asked to do it. </div> </div> </div>They seem pretty done with their part in it.<br /> <br /> And it's fine if you more or less consider anything after the 1e core to have been basically a mistake, have the Anarchs as a favorite sect that you feel were wronged, what have you. If you don't feel those things, you probably think it was kind of a bad thing. When there are dev comments to the tune of saying that it's actually good when an rpg goes hyper specific and gives you less options, erhm. If you liked options, you're SOL but for fan content you're going to have to climb a hill to convince new groups on.<br /> <br /> V5 will continue to do its thing, which amongst other things at this point (outside of the videogames and what have you) is basically be a table top rpg product line shepherded by some people in their late 40s and verging 50s with a very narrow view on how VtM should be played, who want people in their 20s to be under the impression that this frankly very old take on this game is the new sexy perfected form of VtM. When they call anything in the middle of that &quot;legacy gaming&quot; in a way that feels like &quot;go away into that corner&quot;, or talk about how that book someone liked only existed because of &quot;the supplement treadmill&quot;, the vibe for the gameline is a condescending one at best.<br /> <br /> And it's almost comforting how not new that is either, in a warped way? VtM (honestly the entire WoD) has spent almost its entire existence from the jump being written by people holding various chunks of its player base in contempt for how they play VtM. It just felt easier to previously ignore said vibe. (Granted Gehenna has an actual paragraph in one of its endings dedicated to saying &quot;You, Yes You, The Person Reading This Book, Were Playing This Game Wrong The Whole Time&quot;, almost like some kind of &quot;What if the Neverending Story hated you?&quot; trip. But it was at the time the end of VtM, it was pretty ignorable when I was already looking forward to VtR in them days ;p)<br /> <br /> But it is what it is, this is the line going forward. Anyone with a problem with that will ultimately age out of the audience/gaming.<br /> <br /> On a corporate level, the main thing that matters is that the videogames make some kind of money (and even moderate videogame money is wildly beyond ttrpg money, unless you are Dungeons and Dragons, or, I don't know, CoC in Japan maybe? It's apparently very big in Japan.) Though obviously that otherwise the ttrpg line of books isn't some actual money sink has to have some level of importance. Corporations don't like to lose money. And when Paradox certainly seems to want other companies to buy into and develop this IP, &quot;well it is based on this failing ttrpg line&quot; would not be a good look. So at the very least, the ttrpg line is probably doing okay by its own standards, even as the videogame efforts look increasingly like a fluke-y mess.<br /> <br /> To be topical though, the thing that stands out to me for the success of Bloodhunt is that should anyone come from that to the role playing game (not always a guarantee. Some of Bloodlines own following seemed to barely intersect with, be aware of, or care about the ttrpg, but who even knows), they'll be met with a game that turns up its nose and says &quot;combat should not be more than three rounds, but if you smell and don't understand good gaming, you can use the optional rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the idea that VtM as a table top roleplaying game now needs to stay how it is to be &quot;adaptation friendly&quot;, then that definitely fell right down. Its most successful adaptation to date is a battle royale. The game said battle royale is based on hates the idea of combat lasting more than three rounds (with said three rounds followed by a narrated conclusion as needed.)<br /> <br /> That's not just a mechanical thing. The game that Bloodhunt the videogame is has not all that fundamentally much to do with the game VtM 5th vocally insists it is, just from simple mission statements of &quot;what happens in this world and how do you, then person using this game, play out these things that happen.&quot; There is a considerable distance between the two and that makes the VtM world details feel not especially important beyond &quot;thin patina put over you trying to murder circus all the other players around you, but this time when you do it, you're a vampire and are using vampire powers!&quot; Saying &quot;so and so setting focus made it easier to adapt&quot;, it's hard to see. &quot;You are a vampire and are killing everyone around you with your awesome badass vampire powers. Drink people's blood! Avoid red mist!&quot; can ignore or exist in spite of whatever any detail, deep or shallow.<br /> <br /> The Hunter the Reckoning video game was successful enough to spawn sequels and different console releases (of dubious quality one grants, but the first one made enough money to push all that). And yet the lore and thematics of HtR ran miles deep. Did that matter? Did it feel like anyone truly cared when making it? Did that actually get in the way? Did HtR the video game really in any meaningful sense especially resemble HtR the ttrpg or was it just a thing it mugged whatever detail it liked from, changed anything it didn't, and didn't give a crap about the rest? (I mean the video game definitely resembled the otherwise totally not matching the gameplay artwork from the corebook, sure. Otherwise?) &quot;Hey, this thing is about humans with powers killing monsters!&quot;, boom, game. Hunter existed because the studio was full of WoD fans and HtR had an action sounding premise if you could and did ignore the finer details of it. By the time HtR production started, that gameline had a relatively sizable pile of complicated of lore. It clearly didn't get in the way. &quot;Adaptation friendliness&quot; feels like a mirage in that sense as far as thinking it is something that the ttrpg's current shape makes possible.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, for a wildly more successful example, the big two company superhero comics are some of the bar none least simple comprehension friendly nerd genre mediums out there if you look at them. Especially Marvel! DC at least halfheartedly tries to reboot their comics every 5-10 years after '86 (totally incompetently, but still). Marvel keeps insisting everything from the 60s to right now is still an ongoing canon narrative of increasingly convoluted density and minutiae. And yet, the MCU happened, and it gleefully picked and chose at times seeming randomly from what material it wanted to bother with, undaunted. The results made a ton of bank.<br /> <br /> We're otherwise diving deeply into tautology times to put forward that the conveniently VtM ttrpg setting closest to what you want VtM on the whole to be is the best VtM for adapting. There's a whole lot of successful* on a scale VtM never touched vampire media that works/worked off culture/organizations/narrative that don't particularly resemble &quot;scrappy Anarchs vs the Man.&quot; To the point that if someone wants to say &quot;I'm not aware of such&quot; in reply, I don't know if I can really engage with that. It requires eyeballing a chunk of various forms of media and going &quot;those didn't exist&quot;. VtM 5th exists in tabletop form how it exists because that is the way the people in charge of its writing decisions it like Vampire the Masquerade to be. That other vampire themed efforts have been successful just fine despite having very little thematic resonance with VtM 5th demonstrates that this is not some above perfect mass market formula they hit on. You can present vampire stories and worlds in other ways than VtM emphasizes and apparently do quite well for the choice. The developers didn't need it to be this way, they chose it to be this way, and they executed some highly successful and extensive promotional efforts to sell their potential audience on those choices. There is at least a solid enough core in the game to hang that promotion on, absolutely. But that's all that means. The idea that these changes or reversions or however you want to view it to VtM's presentation are crucial or otherwise it wouldn't be friendly to adapt or understand or etc is not borne out by just.. the history of vampire related media up and down whatever all method of delivery of that media.<br /> <br /> VtM could have been just fine &quot;this is the story of ornate societies in a secret world beyond the known one and the people who are part of those societies&quot; as opposed to &quot;this is the story of a small group of disorganized outsiders interacting with a secret world that is bad on almost all levels, and becoming part of its ornate details is a bad thing bad people do, not our heroes.&quot; Genre material, vampires all entirely aside, has done both these things or even mixed them up, and been successful fine either way. I need to believe no one needs examples of these things, because we are all nerds having a discussion about genre material on an extremely niche forum, dedicated to a niche corner, of a niche industry. I feel like this is at least something I can note as stuff having existed, and people being able to recall all that stuff in terms of non reality based media just fine. I will otherwise have a sad, as the kids say (or probably stopped saying by now). I will have a terrible sad indeed.<br /> <br /> Though, y'know, speaking of Vampire media that was popular at one time or another. One of the things that always got me about a variety of popular at one point or another vampire media vs VtM for the entire existence of the gameline, is how sizable chunks of it are about old as hell vampires and how much of VtM tries to explode your head like that scene from Scanners if you so much as think about wanting to play old as hell vampires.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know, Elysium happened. If you look at that book and tell me it didn't exist as grudgingly and punitively as possible, well, opinions vary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Please note the word I used here is successful. Successful doesn't mean good. Successful doesn't mean you like it. If you want to argue that whatever successful vampire thing that doesn't resemble V5 was bad in terms of quality, that has nothing to do with successful. Hell, I think V5 with a few exceptions is mostly bad, in a quality sense. And clearly I don't really care for it, outside of a small handful of things. That doesn't mean I think it isn't successful. We're four years into this gameline at this point. Unless secret corporate ninja magic is going on (and, come on, it's not), V5 has to have been at least moderately successful as a table top roleplaying game. That is not a thing I think that can be denied at this point in table top roleplaying terms. I can't really believe they're putting out these books or licensing them to other ttrpg publishing companies or what have you at a loss. Certainly not for four years. That would be baffling.<br /> <br /> Though, sure, in a sense of the company that wants this IP to make videogames money, or hit other bigger than ttrpg money sources, I will grant things look dicey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  elaborating on a statement for clarity 07-20-2022, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T23:17:15-07:00","id":1487111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487109#post1487109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything tabletop rpg related not from OPP, and that seems to be basically everything onwards for V5 at this point (unless you've read something I personally missed), has them as more or less incompetent or diabolical (or both) cartoon villains that come with a borderline lecture that selecting this play option makes you bad as a person, or certainly at least one that has bad ideas about gaming. Honestly, other than Chicago by Night itself and its direct spinoffs, where do you get &quot;kind of awesome&quot; from? That's the main OPP book with a major Camarilla focus (and the direct spinoffs it has), the others that exist focus on other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my opinion on the subject is different than many readers because I buy virtually everything that has the WOD label with it. Which gives me a slightly different view than those who are only familiar with the book results.<br /> <br /> So, my opinion adds:<br /> <br /> * <b>The Fall of London</b>: You can side with the Camarilla and become Prince of London if you go against Lady Anne as well as siding with Lady Anne (which I would never do because why serve when you can rule?). There's no Anarch option either.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Choice of Games</b>: Of the three WOD games (there may be four now actually), NIGHT ROAD has a reasonable &quot;cool&quot; prince you can side with. PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES is also a Camarilla-heavy game.<br /> <br /> * <b>Blood Hunt</b>: You can side with the Camarilla in this book agaisnt the Anarch.<br /> <br /> * <b>Winter's Teeth</b>: Cecily Bane is one of the Camarilla's deputies despite being a former Anarch as well as eventually ascends to become Prince.<br /> <br /> * <b>Coteries of New York/Shadows of New York</b>: You cannot actually side with the Anarchs in these games. You have to side with the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T23:54:04-07:00","id":1487115,"title":"","content":"Just as a quick add on rather than to re-edit, since I mentioned superhero comics to live action movie adaptations. Did you know the movie Logan is in fact adapted from a story from the comics (a frankly bad and overrated arc of comics in my own view)? A movie that in final result almost completely resembles nothing from its source material? Logan owes as much to the Western Shane as it does Old Man Logan, which as &quot;adaptation friendliness&quot; goes, includes such details as the Hulk committing incest-rape on She Hulk to found a clan of inbred hillbilly Hulks. There are references otherwise in the comics story that run ludicrously deep at times. <br /> <br /> The movie somehow found a way around this and a wide variety of other finely ground or gross ass things or both to tell the story it wanted to tell. In fact it goes so far as to yoink and mass alter characters from other entirely different stories that had nothing to do with Old Man Logan, stories and characters that are themselves convoluted right out to nonsense.<br /> <br /> And yet, without said comics, the movie would not exist.<br /> <br /> Adaptation friendliness really does feel like a mirage. If a game developer/film or television producer/whatever sees even a conceptual germ of something they like in a thing, or more importantly, can sell, all the details surrounding that thing did not stop them from seeing it.<br /> <br /> (Also, Shane itself is based on a 1949 novel that it took a few liberties with. And Laura from Logan is herself a riff off of X-23, who first appeared in the cartoon X-men Evolution, that was itself a loose adaptation of various X-men comics. She was then brought into the comics themselves as a character after the cartoon, which is where she was noticed by the people who made Logan, to include in their movie. And if you could follow that entire chain of who was adapted from what to where to make a given end result, congratulations, you're ready to watch Tenet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or just understand that adaptation friendliness is a thin concept as far as making it more likely something will be adapted and be successful at being adapted).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T00:17:07-07:00","id":1487116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487111#post1487111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think my opinion on the subject is different than many readers because I buy virtually everything that has the WOD label with it. Which gives me a slightly different view than those who are only familiar with the book results.<br /> <br /> So, my opinion adds:<br /> <br /> * <b>The Fall of London</b>: You can side with the Camarilla and become Prince of London if you go against Lady Anne as well as siding with Lady Anne (which I would never do because why serve when you can rule?). There's no Anarch option either.<br /> <br /> * <b>The Choice of Games</b>: Of the three WOD games (there may be four now actually), NIGHT ROAD has a reasonable &quot;cool&quot; prince you can side with. PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES is also a Camarilla-heavy game.<br /> <br /> * <b>Blood Hunt</b>: You can side with the Camarilla in this book agaisnt the Anarch.<br /> <br /> * <b>Winter's Teeth</b>: Cecily Bane is one of the Camarilla's deputies despite being a former Anarch as well as eventually ascends to become Prince.<br /> <br /> * <b>Coteries of New York/Shadows of New York</b>: You cannot actually side with the Anarchs in these games. You have to side with the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked you where you got &quot;kind of awesome&quot; from, not &quot;you can play the Camarilla&quot;. You can play the Camarilla in from the book V5 too, you're just hammered over the head with that you are siding with evil, morons, or more usually evil morons.<br /> <br /> Winter's Teeth has Cecily Bane trick the Caitiff she took in into straight up murdering an innocent person she picked out to be murdered by them, then showing them that she did, just to &quot;teach her a lesson about being a vampire&quot; (yes, the Caitiff is herself a pile of crap, that doesn't really change the excessiveness of it all), and otherwise has the Camarilla nearly get obliterated by perhaps the stupidest, least subtle hunters ever, down to &quot;Gangrel primogen attempts badass rant, is then immediately rocket launchered to death for what seems to mostly be comedic reasons.&quot; The Camarilla are an endless circle of petty backstabbing, incompetence and utterly needless monstrosity in Winter's Teeth to the point of verging on bad comedy routine versions of how the Sabbat Lasombra used to be described. But hey, Ian Carfax was cool for half a second before then launching into one of the truly dumbest plans I have ever beheld in the sequel series. &quot;I will somehow leverage werewolves into teaching me special knowledge by threatening their sacred spaces. This is a plan I think will work, on werewolves, despite the entire history of interaction between werewolves and vampires. I am a Tremere justicar.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bloodhunt is a battle royale game about killing everybody with your cool vampire powers, the details beyond that are kinda incidental.<br /> <br /> Coteries of New York you say? Let's talk about Shadows of New York then, where the more or less &quot;good person ending&quot; has you rejecting the Camarilla and getting the hell out of New York with your girlfriend. The &quot;become primogen&quot; ending is the Gro- Uhhh, Julia Was The Monster At The End Of The Book ending. It even centers around covering up the death of an Anarch, no less.<br /> <br /> And Fall of London is one of the few V5 era books that an otherwise fractious feeling online fanbase can agree on is crap and seemed to help cost the licensor at the time the franchise. &quot;You play the Camarilla in this terrible supplement&quot; is not &quot;the Camarilla are bad, but it's okay, because they're still kind of awesome&quot;.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I am responding to this, the thing I directly quoted from you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>* </i><b>Camarilla</b><i>: Snooty. Bad. But still sexy and kind of awesome</i> </div> </div> </div>In responding to it, I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anything tabletop rpg related not from OPP, and that seems to be basically everything onwards for V5 at this point (unless you've read something I personally missed), has them as more or less incompetent or diabolical (or both) cartoon villains that come with a borderline lecture that selecting this play option makes you bad as a person, or certainly at least one that has bad ideas about gaming. Honestly, other than Chicago by Night itself and its direct spinoffs, where do you get &quot;kind of awesome&quot; from? That's the main OPP book with a major Camarilla focus (and the direct spinoffs it has), the others that exist focus on other things. </div> </div> </div>Telling me &quot;you play the Camarilla in these things&quot; does not show this thing you said. I remain comfortable with that V5's non OPP take on the Camarilla boils down to &quot;evil, idiots, and very often evil idiots. When you side with them, you are shown being evil, an idiot, or both. The cool kids are the heroic Anarchs.&quot;<br /> <br /> More to the point, as far as Night Road and its ilk, you're the one that made this thread to talk about how Bloodhunt is the only successful videogame to this point. &quot;You can play the Camarilla in these things where they are either terrible, or the medium you are playing them in itself is terrible&quot; is not making your case very well.<br /> <br /> You said &quot;the Camarilla are still kind of awesome&quot;. Where do you feel this is the case that is not Chicago by Night and its ancillary material? In what particular way do you think this is so?<br /> <br /> edit: I mean I guess for the visual novel/games if you're trying to say &quot;well they weren't well received, but they were still good&quot;... sure? That's basically a handful of minor things then, and also glosses over things like Shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T00:26:27-07:00","id":1487117,"title":"","content":"I think our disagreement is in the fact that being part of the Camarilla and being evil doesn't make playing them less awesome.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> I consider part of the Camarilla's major appeal to be one of the hidden masters of society and utterly lacking in morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T00:38:44-07:00","id":1487118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487117#post1487117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think our disagreement is in the fact that being part of the Camarilla and being evil doesn't make playing them less awesome.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> I consider part of the Camarilla's major appeal to be one of the hidden masters of society and utterly lacking in morality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no problems with the Camarilla being evil. Every vampire sect has a core of hypocritical rot and malign intent that festers within it that the members of that sect have to decide how they will deal with, or not and how they will live with the decision of &quot;or not&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have problems with the Camarilla being so evil it makes them look like cartoonish morons. Like an exaggerated caricature. You seem to want to reduce my observation to &quot;you're just being salty because the Camarilla aren't heroic.&quot;<br /> <br /> No, I'm being salty because a thing that used to have nuance, now has none, and I like nuance. Also when that is combined with pretty thorough ineptitude, the statement on something you might otherwise want to play, feels pretty clear.<br /> <br /> In what way do you feel the Camarilla has been portrayed in V5 as &quot;awesome&quot; that isn't more or less one and a half books by a publisher who isn't doing more books? What specific circumstances?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, they're pretty questionable at being hidden masters of society in V5. That's one of the whole points of V5, that their attempt at hidden mastery fell right to pieces, be it from their own internal self sabotage via elder games, or their own overconfident overreach. Camarilla as failure is one of the reasons the V5 plot moves along.<br /> <br /> So again, morons, evil, or evil morons.<br /> <br /> Edit edit: If it helps, I will lean into my argument being reduced to its simplest terms. Forget awesome, we can stick a pin in awesome and come back to it later. Where as an organization do you feel the Camarilla was portrayed even as competent? Again, not Chicago by Night+kickstarter extras.<br /> <br /> And if you're going to say Winter's Teeth, Cecily Bane having the Twin City's Camarilla's one brain cell (and frankly she got by on sheer luck at points) does not make the Camarilla look competent. It makes her look like the writing people gripe about Batman getting in the comics sometimes, where to make him look good, everyone around him has their IQ drop a thousand points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:03:23-07:00","id":1487122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487101#post1487101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understand this is just my theory but I believe Paradox Interactive is currently doing the majority of things it's doing for the purposes of spreading the IP around. They've signed deals for World of Darkness movies and television shows. They also DO want to make the massively successful (hopefully) Bloodlines 2 and perhaps more games of its like.<br /> <br /> Everything else is really just advertising for these. I think they overestimated how much popularity the 20 year old World of Darkness IP had inside the United States and perhaps outside of it so a lot of what they're doing is based around getting word of mouth out that it alive and well.<br /> <br /> It's why I believe V5 is never going to be amended because the purpose of V5 is to make the most adaptation friendly World of Darkness possible. Which is the following:<br /> <br /> <u><b>V5 as a Story Bible</b></u><br /> <br /> * <b>Anarchs</b>: Good. Scrappy underdog poor kids and street punks.<br /> <br /> * <b>Camarilla</b>: Snooty. Bad. But still sexy and kind of awesome.<br /> <br /> * <b>Sabbat</b>: The scary bad guys you can kill with impunity.<br /> <br /> * <b>Hunters</b>: The government is big, nasty, and scary and out to kill you poor Anarchs when you don't want vampire opponents but just guys with guns. Also, why does the government not intervene? Because they're already hunting you.<br /> <br /> * <b>Clan Changes: </b>Make it all as simplified and straightforward as you need.<br /> <br /> *<b> Continuity Soft Reboot</b>: Only a handful of spinoffs have any reference to older canon.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, I don't think this is a BAD thing necessarily but it could have been handled MUCH-MUCH better and OPP pretty much should have been asked to do it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fail to see how the anarchs are supposed to be the &quot;good&quot; guys of the setting when they are just as relentlessly horrible as the Camarilla and possibly even more stupid (the anarchs book is a good example of this), the fact that they had to do the other sects dirty (especially the sabbat) to prop them up and still fail miserably should tell you how utterly inconsequential they always were in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla lost most of what made it &quot;sexy and awesome&quot; when they decided to reduce the collective neural capacity of the sect members, they fact that they decided to amp their dickishness didn't help, going by the camarilla book, they felt more like the sabbat at certain points.<br /> <br /> The sabbat got the worst out of the deal and turned into monodimensional assholes who are used to make the other vampires (who barely better then them) appear just a smidge less horrible, all the complexities and layers of the sect just flushed down the drain to get a cheap antagonist.<br /> <br /> Hunters could have been really awesome if they didn't make them into psychopats ready to torch buildings to kill a single vampire, again no complexities here just cheap antagonists evil enough that you don't fill bad when you kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:18:25-07:00","id":1487126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487122#post1487122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how the anarchs are supposed to be the &quot;good&quot; guys of the setting when they are just as relentlessly horrible as the Camarilla and possibly even more stupid (the anarchs book is a good example of this), the fact that they had to do the other sects dirty (especially the sabbat) to prop them up and still fail miserably should tell you how utterly inconsequential they always were in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't begrudge you your hatred of the Anarchs but I should point out something that a lot of people who hate the Anarchs do seem to miss:<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are just Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They're a particularly extreme sect of them but let's not pretend they're anything more than an extreme and effective sect of them. They exist to overthrow the Elders, the Antediluvians especially, and engage in all the same violent revolutionary rhetoric as well as terrorism as the Anarchs because they are Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They will never be anything more because their identity is Anarchs in total war as well as rejecting Humanity.<br /> <br /> They're, indeed, a branch of the OG Anarchs.<br /> <br /> If you remove the Anarch philosophy from the Sabbat, they have nothing.<br /> <br /> Whenever people complain about the Anarchs vs, the Sabbat, IMHO, they are actually just complaining about the fact that there's a moderate non-extremist branch of Anarchs that seeks compromise or non-diablerie solutions to the Elders.<br /> <br /> The entire metaplot of the game is about the conflict between the Anarchs and Camarilla. It's just the Sabbat are the cool ones of the former. It's why they're my second favorite sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:43:46-07:00","id":1487130,"title":"","content":"Funny, if you think about it, the OG Anarchs were the Antedeluvians themselves when they were 'young', banded together and rose up against and owerthrown/destroyed their Elders<br /> And the most prominent Sabbat leaders are actually older than the Inner Circle mebers of the Camarilla, veteran elders, some times methuselahs themselves of not &quot;worse&quot;<br /> WoD have a knack for Irony","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:49:17-07:00","id":1487131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487130#post1487130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, if you think about it, the OG Anarchs were the Antedeluvians themselves when they were 'young', banded together and rose up against and owerthrown/destroyed their Elders<br /> And the most prominent Sabbat leaders are actually older than the Inner Circle mebers of the Camarilla, veteran elders, some times methuselahs themselves of not &quot;worse&quot;<br /> WoD have a knack for Irony</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the War of Ages is a central theme of the game. I'm not sure if it was a literal Curse of Caine but vampires are destined to slay their Elders and the Elders to oppress the young.<br /> <br /> And part of the fun of the Sabbat is when your PC figures out, &quot;Wait a minute, we're an army. Since when is an ARMY free?&quot;<br /> <br /> One of my all-time favorite PC journeys was when we played out the Transylvania Chronicles as the Sabbat only for him to realize in Modern Nights right before Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://y.yarn.co/e66b9a36-95af-4587-92ea-3ea6172580d7_text.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T02:26:53-07:00","id":1487137,"title":"","content":"I'll try to be even more clear about something to get around the whole reductive &quot;you just can't handle depiction of evil&quot; implication that seems to be regularly trotted out when the discourse leans this way.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, certainly from when I preferred the writing for it, is an ornate machine that kills innocent people by routine. Far less monstrously than the Sabbat, certainly, and by far less frequently, but still horribly. The Camarilla as an organization has accepted that hey, gots to keep that Masquerade, and if that means people gotta die, welp! And the insidiousness of the Camarilla is they can make that sound reasonable. Do you want the Masquerade to drop and the world to light on fire and you and everyone you feel feelings for to die? No? Well then, this is one of those egg breaking omelets childe.<br /> <br /> And once you accept that awfulness into yourself, the other bits start coming down the line as though they were waiting for you to open the door into your soul. Oh, someone accidentally killed their vessel? Well it's not like that happens <i>too</i> often, it's not like we're engaged in Sabbat style bloodbaths here. And don't you want the Tower to stay fed, and strong? What if it stops being strong? Are you ready to deal with that? Are you ready for the world to break? Of course you're not. And you know how much worse it could be, don't you? You feel that snarling within you, you feel that hunger. We built an entire world out of chains just so you could wrap those chains around it, childe. Just so you still have a way to go through the motions and have one, or two, or even three moments every so often where those motions mean something. Play the games, and play along, and we'll all be chained together. Yes of course some more lightly than others. You want to hold onto your humanity, don't you childe? Tell me what about the human experience was ever <i>fair</i>. Now bow.<br /> <br /> The evil of the Camarilla as I prefer it, is an evil of expediency that cloaks itself in stylized politics and even ideals so that you can tell yourself it's too big to do anything but live within. Order and society writ so large, yet so rationalized you can convince yourself it has a meaning larger than you and that you didn't do so blindly, that you work for it, but just as importantly, it works for you. Instead of acknowledging that it is feeding on the meaning you give it. That you can tell yourself it is so powerful that really, you had no good choice. An evil of all the horrible little compromises you make because they made sense to make, and only when its too late do you step back and realize the mountain of wretchedness all those compromises have built, and the worst thing of all is the knowledge that it hasn't killed you, either in body or in soul. That you truly could keep going this way forever, because there's always <i>just</i> <i>enough </i>of you left over to hold on at the end of the night when the dance, be it played out in a salon or a sewer, stops for another sunrise. The evil of the Camarilla comes of all the people who accepted &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest A Beast I Become&quot; without even really trying to shout back a no, and instead reaching angrily to violently pull down anyone who does shout to trudge back with them through the mire. And then getting just enough of a reassuring &quot;hey, good job&quot; pat on the back for that motion from the people who set the whole thing going in the first place.<br /> <br /> And all knowing in their hearts that all that is, for a certain use of the word, true, they react in different ways. Some embrace the games, or even worse, the corruption and the feuds, the climb and hoarding of power, because even the biggest loser gets a moment they can tell themselves is a win, and look! It's those one or two or three moments that you tell yourself meant something, that you felt something. Some do the best they think that can to use the system for something actually resembling its own right sounding delusions, even as that system compromises them, hoping that if they achieve even one good thing for someone they care about, or even better, someone they don't care about, that it will be worth all the awful things, worth knowing the Tower grinds the people who push too hard from within it into nothing. Some are just trying to <i>live</i> and can't you understand they're just trying to live? Can't you let them just have five goddamned minutes to live their (un)life? And most are all these things at one point or another, because even with a Beast, the thing about being still human, about even just giving lip service to the idea of your humanity like a good little Camarilla would, is humans are a mess, and terrified of that messiness. And they will go to great and terrible lengths not to face it, to feel safe from it, and give great and terrible power to something that will let them live with it from one night to the next. The Camarilla asks for so little! Just let it rule you, and you can have everything you really want.<br /> <br /> Look, you asked to be protected, and the Camarilla protected you. You cowered before the Tower; it was frightening. It has put its hand on history, it has turned the mortal world to its will, and it has done it all for <i>you</i>. Frankly the Camarilla is <i>exhausted</i> from living up to your expectations. Hasn't it been generous?<br /> <br /> Now bow.<br /> <br /> And get rid of that body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Direly overwrought ultra amateur prose and Jareth paraphrases aside, this is not an evil that, y'know, *works* with the balkanized, moron, half assed crime family, evil for evil's sake Camarilla. There needs to be enough of a measure of power and competence that there is an actual sacrifice and challenge in not going with its flow, even just long enough to do one good thing, for however long it lasts, even knowing that you'll end up right back where you were within the Tower. There needs to be that sense of noir (and I think the game lost a lot for having thrown its sense of film noir over the side). There needs to be enough depth to playing its games that you can tell yourself there is a reward for the fleeting moments of when you win them, even at the horrible costs of doing so. The world without them needs to feel like it could scare you enough that you turn your face away from the world, and back to the Tower. The evil of the Sabbat is in your face, or certainly at least more openly jarring. The evil of the Camarilla is the ending of the Godfather when the doors close in front of Kay as she is helpless to do anything but be shut out from how far Michael has fallen and yet somehow still functions under a mask of humanity, and his having rationalized every single step that took them to that point. To be pulled in that deep requires there be something compelling about the pull, even and especially when you know that pull is a lie that gets stronger when you believe it.<br /> <br /> There is otherwise something vital to the Camarilla as far as being this ornate global thing that has the sheer gall to say &quot;all vampires are us&quot; and to pull it off enough that their enemies blink for even just half a second of &quot;oh shit, maybe they are?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla needs to actually have some moments of symbolizing something in the first place so that symbol can be shown to be hollow. It needs to have ideals, even warped ones, so that it can be shown to be grotesque hypocrites about them. &quot;Can I work with this? Can I force this thing to work for me? Is the mistake even asking these questions in the first place and not getting into the goddamn car with my mortal girlfriend and taking my chances?&quot; doesn't work if the Camarilla is too pathetic, unsubtle, or just inane to make someone have that struggle.<br /> <br /> And on a much, much, much less serious note? I <i>like</i> ultra stylized sociopolitical gaming with vampires. When there's evil in that, I'd prefer evil in those terms. That's enjoyable for me. When the Camarilla are just a cluster of vindictive clowns in a shattered world, that feeling falls riiiiight apart into nothing.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, that bit with Cecily Banes and the Caitiff? It's dumb excess for the sake of being dumb excess. It's just shock value trying to act like it is being deep. It's what people who dislike the Sabbat, reduce the Sabbat to being when they talk about why they believe the Sabbat are dumb. It's what people mock M. Night Shyamalan's &quot;what a twist!&quot; endings for. &quot;LOL, I tricked you into killing an innocent person in a way that makes the lives of the people they care about worse also, lololol! Lessonz!! (tm)&quot; There are so many other ways that could have been done. And when it comes in a series where the Camarilla are otherwise pretty much a bunch of backstabbing dolts who at times get killed for a joke, I mean, sure, but don't expect me to invest in any of it. If this is where someone wants to trot out &quot;well it's supposed to be satire&quot;, well again, hey sure, but that has nothing to do with my being unable to &quot;view the Camarilla as evil&quot; and more to do then with my making a mistake of taking the game at its word when it told me I could do more with it than laugh at the dumb dumbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T02:56:18-07:00","id":1487140,"title":"","content":"For me, I've always felt the Camarilla benefited from not remotely attempting to lie to its members. There's no ideology to the Camarilla, no claim ot being the good guy, and no attempt to manipulate the masses into believing it is anything more than what it is and that actually makes it refreshing to any vampire over the age of Neonate.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is a mob and everything flows up.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla states bluntly that you are a member of it, you are bound to follow its rules, and the purpose of it is the following:<br /> <br /> * To protect the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> * To protect its richer more powerful oldest members.<br /> <br /> For most of human history and arguably now, there's no need to explain WHY the upper class are the upper class. They are because they are and the system exists to protect THEM not you. The Camarilla is slightly better than historical feudalism, though, because it DOES provide the stability of the Masquerade and covering up for idiots.<br /> <br /> It also has a slim-slim promise: That you might, eventually, rise up to power yourself if you live long enough. Then YOU will be kicking around your lessers.<br /> <br /> In the RL mafia, money all flows upward. That's why you're obedient because you want to work for a decade to become a made man (if you have the right pedigree) or, if you don't, to at least get your own solid position in the organization. The organization makes it clear this is about power and prestige and that's enough for 99% of people.<br /> <br /> It's like asking why a person joins a brutal unforgiving corporation. &quot;Because you need money.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:03:07-07:00","id":1487141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487126#post1487126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't begrudge you your hatred of the Anarchs but I should point out something that a lot of people who hate the Anarchs do seem to miss:<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are just Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They're a particularly extreme sect of them but let's not pretend they're anything more than an extreme and effective sect of them. They exist to overthrow the Elders, the Antediluvians especially, and engage in all the same violent revolutionary rhetoric as well as terrorism as the Anarchs because they are Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They will never be anything more because their identity is Anarchs in total war as well as rejecting Humanity.<br /> <br /> They're, indeed, a branch of the OG Anarchs.<br /> <br /> If you remove the Anarch philosophy from the Sabbat, they have nothing.<br /> <br /> Whenever people complain about the Anarchs vs, the Sabbat, IMHO, they are actually just complaining about the fact that there's a moderate non-extremist branch of Anarchs that seeks compromise or non-diablerie solutions to the Elders.<br /> <br /> The entire metaplot of the game is about the conflict between the Anarchs and Camarilla. It's just the Sabbat are the cool ones of the former. It's why they're my second favorite sect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By the same highly reductive token as this, the Anarch philosophy boils down to little more than &quot;I do what I want however I want and no one can tell me otherwise&quot; and it's the transformation of the original Anarchs into the Sabbat that allowed them to stop and think about what that actually means as far as transhumanism, as far as something they could exist on with spiritual coherence, as far as not simply fighting to be free, which is the main rationale for why the Anarchs came into being, but what it actually means to have and do something with the freedom of your own existence.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs, from this perspective, became the Sabbat, because the Anarchs offer little to nothing when they don't have something to fight against, because they have little to nothing when someone isn't defining their lives for them, even to shake a fist at, as shown by their eager readiness to turn even on each other.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs came into being, elder manipulations to create them aside, as much to fight for their own survival as anything, being fed into the Inquisition as pawns as they were. The Sabbat later considered the question of &quot;what does being worthy of survival mean?&quot; And the answer they came up with was monstrous and from a human perspective, completely insane, but they certainly put that answer forward.<br /> <br /> Even V5 reflects this in a way. The Anarchs became more spiritual (taking in the Ministry and various cults previous forms of the Movement would have regarded as sickening) because the Anarch way alone holds no meaning or value to sustain an unlife on in the long run, it's just rage and shaking a fist. It's just flare up, burnout, and collapse. The Sabbat went feral because they basically threw over their spiritual side for the pure war of the Gehenna Crusade, banishing any path that got in the way, and taking the most run down versions of the ones that were left. So in V5, the Anarchs became more like the Sabbat, and the Sabbat went back to being nothing more than Anarchs, and as a result became a hollow play of themselves.<br /> <br /> Now, is that a narrow and super reductive take that ignores a variety of material in order to stress a particular reading? Absolutely.<br /> <br /> But so is what you just posted about the Sabbat. You can't think that anyone who is into the sect and dislikes it being made into a narrow, one note, unplayable version of itself would be happy with being told &quot;they're just a variant of the super cool Anarchs anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> Starting a post with &quot;I don't begrudge you your hatred&quot;, then following it up with &quot;but here's why the thing you like is only cool when it is defined by the thing I like&quot;, is not great.<br /> <br /> &quot;The thing you like has nothing without the thing I like.&quot; is... not great.<br /> <br /> When people say they feel like V5 gets condescending, this is the sort of vibe it has. You say a lot of times how much you in fact like the Sabbat and how much you don't like that they're unplayable but you seem to miss that people are expressing both that they don't like that the Sabbat is unplayable, and they don't like how much of a narrow stereotype of itself it was turned into, from how it was previously written.<br /> <br /> A reply that says they are in fact a narrow stereotype with little to sustain them on isn't saying &quot;they're my second favorite sect&quot;, it's mostly saying &quot;this thing you like has no value and it's mostly that I just hate the Camarilla that they're #2&quot;. At the very least that's how it reads.<br /> <br /> &quot;I actually like the Sabbat. But also they're a glorified subsect with nothing to sustain them.&quot; are not statements that fit together well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:04:47-07:00","id":1487142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487137#post1487137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is otherwise something vital to the Camarilla as far as being this ornate global thing that has the sheer gall to say &quot;all vampires are us&quot; and to pull it off enough that their enemies blink for even just half a second of &quot;oh shit, maybe they are?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly! &quot;Overwrought amateur prose&quot; or not, that whole post was still a fun read, and describes precisely what I want, no, what I <i>need</i> the Camarilla to be in my chronicles. Good job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:12:15-07:00","id":1487144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487142#post1487142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, exactly! &quot;Overwrought amateur prose&quot; or not, that whole post was still a fun read, and describes precisely what I want, no, what I <i>need</i> the Camarilla to be in my chronicles. Good job!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aw, thank you. It was pretty spur of the moment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:17:27-07:00","id":1487145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487140#post1487140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I've always felt the Camarilla benefited from not remotely attempting to lie to its members. There's no ideology to the Camarilla, no claim ot being the good guy, and no attempt to manipulate the masses into believing it is anything more than what it is and that actually makes it refreshing to any vampire over the age of Neonate.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is a mob and everything flows up.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla states bluntly that you are a member of it, you are bound to follow its rules, and the purpose of it is the following:<br /> <br /> * To protect the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> * To protect its richer more powerful oldest members.<br /> <br /> For most of human history and arguably now, there's no need to explain WHY the upper class are the upper class. They are because they are and the system exists to protect THEM not you. The Camarilla is slightly better than historical feudalism, though, because it DOES provide the stability of the Masquerade and covering up for idiots.<br /> <br /> It also has a slim-slim promise: That you might, eventually, rise up to power yourself if you live long enough. Then YOU will be kicking around your lessers.<br /> <br /> In the RL mafia, money all flows upward. That's why you're obedient because you want to work for a decade to become a made man (if you have the right pedigree) or, if you don't, to at least get your own solid position in the organization. The organization makes it clear this is about power and prestige and that's enough for 99% of people.<br /> <br /> It's like asking why a person joins a brutal unforgiving corporation. &quot;Because you need money.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once upon a time the game had room for the thing you need to be how the Camarilla is written and the way I prefer the Camarilla to be written.<br /> <br /> Now it doesn't, and going forward I'm prettty sure it won't.<br /> <br /> Regardless, casting that as &quot;I understand real life evil better than you&quot;, it's not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:29:07-07:00","id":1487150,"title":"","content":"FYI - Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> for discussing the subject with me in depth, I'm having a lot of fun and hope you are too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487141#post1487141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same highly reductive token as this, the Anarch philosophy boils down to little more than &quot;I do what I want however I want and no one can tell me otherwise&quot; and it's the transformation of the original Anarchs into the Sabbat that allowed them to stop and think about what that actually means as far as transhumanism, as far as something they could exist on with spiritual coherence, as far as not simply fighting to be free, which is the main rationale for why the Anarchs came into being, but what it actually means to have and do something with the freedom of your own existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the large problems with the Anarchs in the setting is the fact it is a broad tent that has dozens of factions underneath its banner but very little development of these factions aside from the Sabbat. They really could have had something with the Brujah Council, French Revolutionaries, and so on but they've really devoited very little effort to making them come alive. I would personally love an Anarch Society book that brings various Anarch groups to life.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Free States is certainly one group but it should hardly be the only one. OPP did more to develop the Anarchs by stating Marcus Vitel is now one of their leaders and has a New Roman Vampire society in Washington DC in one paragraph than many developers have ever tried to.<br /> <br /> But if I were the developer of V5, I would have had this book alongside a restoration of the Old Sabbat or at least a breakaway group that was doing most of their old actions. Reducing the Sabbat to one-dimensional cannon fodder doesn't make the game better, it makes it smaller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs, from this perspective, became the Sabbat, because the Anarchs offer little to nothing when they don't have something to fight against, because they have little to nothing when someone isn't defining their lives for them, even to shake a fist at, as shown by their eager readiness to turn even on each other.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs came into being, elder manipulations to create them aside, as much to fight for their own survival as anything, being fed into the Inquisition as pawns as they were. The Sabbat later considered the question of &quot;what does being worthy of survival mean?&quot; And the answer they came up with was monstrous<br /> and from a human perspective, completely insane, but they certainly put that answer forward. </div> </div> </div>You don't have to sell me on the Sabbat. I've played many a Chronicle from the Dark Ages onward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even V5 reflects this in a way. The Anarchs became more spiritual (taking in the Ministry and various cults previous forms of the Movement would have regarded as sickening) because the Anarch way alone holds no meaning or value to sustain an unlife on in the long run, it's just rage and shaking a fist. It's just flare up, burnout, and collapse. The Sabbat went feral because they basically threw over their spiritual side for the pure war of the Gehenna Crusade, banishing any path that got in the way, and taking the most run down versions of the ones that were left. So in V5, the Anarchs became more like the Sabbat, and the Sabbat went back to being nothing more than Anarchs, and as a result became a hollow play of themselves. </div> </div> </div>I've mentioned this elsewhere but they basically are setting it up as the Dark Ages in the Modern Times. The Anarchs are becoming more spiritual, more violent, more vicious, and more transhumanist in their nature. Which is a sign that the Anarchs are becoming the Sabbat 2.0. This while the Sabbat is becoming a shallow parody of itself. The Camarilla is also treating the Second Inquisition like the Elders treated the First Inquisition, resulting in people flooding to the Anarchs/New Sabbat. It's supposed to be clever, I think.<br /> <br /> In fact, it feels somewhat obvious and I'm not really all that fond of it. I get what they were going for at least. I feel like making the Anarchs into the Sabbat-Lite isn't really where the line should go, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But so is what you just posted about the Sabbat. You can't think that anyone who is into the sect and dislikes it being made into a narrow, one note, unplayable version of itself would be happy with being told &quot;they're just a variant of the super cool Anarchs anyway.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I feel like that kind of runs head long into the fact I am an Anarch fan who loves the Sabbat and hate what happened to them. In fact, one of my major confusions with the fandom is why it's &quot;Anarchs vs. Sabbat&quot; given that there's absolutely so much in common between the two that people are trying to suggest that benefiting one hurts the other.<br /> <br /> Really, I feel like people have stated the Anarchs have taken the Sabbat's role as the Ivory Tower's sect nemesis (which is true) but the worst thing that happened to the Sabbat is unrelated to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Starting a post with &quot;I don't begrudge you your hatred&quot;, then following it up with &quot;but here's why the thing you like is only cool when it is defined by the thing I like&quot;, is not great. </div> </div> </div>No, I am however saying that it's weird to say you like the Sabbat but hate Anarchs since the Sabbat are Anarchs. Just the really mean ones with the cool transhumanist philosophies. I love the Sabbat's shaking a fist at the Elders and suicidal courage as well as their total rejection of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The thing you like has nothing without the thing I like.&quot; is... not great. </div> </div> </div>It's underscoring the sects relationship that is central the origins of the Sabbat as well as the canon history of the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat as a whole.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, the Sabbat's Storyteller Handbook stated at the very beginning they began their life as extremist Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When people say they feel like V5 gets condescending, this is the sort of vibe it has. You say a lot of times how much you in fact like the Sabbat and how much you don't like that they're unplayable but you seem to miss that people are expressing both that they don't like that the Sabbat is unplayable, and they don't like how much of a narrow stereotype of itself it was turned into, from how it was previously written. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what I'm missing. I hate what was done to the Sabbat and think that it is has made the setting much-much worse as a result.<br /> <br /> Do I have the reputation as the V5 promoter here so much that people assume I just defend everything?<br /> <br /> Serious question.<br /> <br /> I find the &quot;dumbing down&quot; of the Sabbat to be the worst decision of V5 by far. It offends a huge chunk of the fanbase and adds nothing. Maybe you could do a good campaign about how the Sabbat is becoming a feral shadow of its former self but you <u><b>can't do that</b></u> unless you have rules for playing a Sabbat player character.<br /> <br /> At the very least you could have provided rules for the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A reply that says they are in fact a narrow stereotype with little to sustain them on isn't saying &quot;they're my second favorite sect&quot;, it's mostly saying &quot;this thing you like has no value and it's mostly that I just hate the Camarilla that they're #2&quot;. At the very least that's how it reads.<br /> <br /> &quot;I actually like the Sabbat. But also they're a glorified subsect with nothing to sustain them.&quot; are not statements that fit together well. </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that I love the Anarchs and the reason that I love the Sabbat is in large part because that I love the stuff in the Sabbat that is in the Anarchs, which is most of their philosophy only taken to the extreme. I don't believe this is logically inconsistent. Mind you, if you don't think the Anarchs and Sabbat are remotely similar then I can see how this argument would not persuade you.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I actually feel like the Anarch becoming more &quot;Sabbat-like&quot; is a failure of imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:39:54-07:00","id":1487151,"title":"","content":"Personally I've always felt the opposite applied, the Sabbat discredited the anarch movement since they have sincere attempts at praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:40:58-07:00","id":1487152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487117#post1487117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider part of the Camarilla's major appeal to be one of the hidden masters of society and utterly lacking in morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this statement is that the Camarilla champion Humanity as the one true Road and their over-obsession with the Masquerade means that they're actually the biggest conventional moralizers in the setting (I say conventional, because y'know, Path of Blood still counts as a form of &quot;morality&quot;. ) They're certainly no saints but they do have a bottom line that's much higher than most of their adversaries.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cars pollute, contribute to shitty city design, and kill hundreds of thousands of people every year, but are drivers amoral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:43:23-07:00","id":1487153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487151#post1487151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I've always felt the opposite applied, the Sabbat discredited the anarch movement since they have sincere attempts at praxis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that many Anarchs are against Praxis.<br /> <br /> The question of what an Anarch is rebelling against can vary wildly with, &quot;The fact I am not in charge&quot; being a perfectly valid answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487152#post1487152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with this statement is that the Camarilla champion Humanity as the one true Road and their over-obsession with the Masquerade means that they're actually the biggest conventional moralizers in the setting (I say conventional, because y'know, Path of Blood still counts as a form of &quot;morality&quot;. ) They're certainly no saints but they do have a bottom line that's much higher than most of their adversaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Humanity is that they champion it on the pragmatic grounds of &quot;Pretend to be a human so that you don't spook the cattle.&quot; They don't actually support humanity on moral grounds, which is probably why it works.<br /> <br /> An Elder who has a massive blood orgy where everyone is killed afterward is only against the law if it causes the Masquerade to be threatened--as it should be.<br /> <br /> I really liked V20's adjustment of the Humanity scale so vampires could be a lot more evil without losing Humanity.<br /> <br /> Humanity 4 vampires should be able to kill as many humans as they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:47:23-07:00","id":1487154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487145#post1487145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once upon a time the game had room for the thing you need to be how the Camarilla is written and the way I prefer the Camarilla to be written.<br /> <br /> Now it doesn't, and going forward I'm prettty sure it won't.<br /> <br /> Regardless, casting that as &quot;I understand real life evil better than you&quot;, it's not great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am making a comparison between the RL mob and Camarilla, not attempting to insult you.<br /> <br /> I apologize, I am really enjoying this conversation and it's some of my favorite posts done this year. You've done a fantastic job of explaining your position and they're great to read.<br /> <br /> Are you not having fun discussing this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:48:55-07:00","id":1487155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487109#post1487109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 will continue to do its thing, which amongst other things at this point (outside of the videogames and what have you) is basically be a table top rpg product line shepherded by some people in their late 40s and verging 50s with a very narrow view on how VtM should be played, who want people in their 20s to be under the impression that this frankly very old take on this game is the new sexy perfected form of VtM. When they call anything in the middle of that &quot;legacy gaming&quot; in a way that feels like &quot;go away into that corner&quot;, or talk about how that book someone liked only existed because of &quot;the supplement treadmill&quot;, the vibe for the gameline is a condescending one at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think there is something inherently interesting in who is writing the game now, how they view the world, and the ultimate consequence for the nature of the game. Back when <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> was first published, the writers at the time where trying to do something different from the game landscape of the era. Their frame of reference was literature and academia, the monsters were metaphorical, and the challenges faced by the players revolved around characters and interpersonal drama. There is a reason why a number of the characters in the first edition of <i>Chicago by Night</i> were derived from characters in <i>The Jungle</i>, and one gets the sense that the author hadn't merely read the book for the purposes of research.<br /> <br /> Of course, it didn't always work, but this was something fresh and different, and fascinating to anyone who had started out with mainstream games. Those of us who were young at the time played these games, became invested in the universe, and made the World of Darkness into one of the great sales success it was during the 1990s. <br /> <br /> And then we grew up.<br /> <br /> In my case, I worked, completed a PhD, and ended up working for a very large commercial organisation. I read actual literary works, and write material for my employer which is more widely consumed than the average V5 supplement. I do write <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> supplements for the Storyteller's Vault in my spare time, as it is a break from the super-serious work I actually do for proper money. I see the flaws of the old White Wolf books more readily than I did when they were first published, but also see the intellectual and creative potential. Which is why I sometimes post on this forum.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I feel that the people who take the professional lead in the game have taken a very different path. They have been very immersed in the gaming scene for decades; their frame of reference for the world are the supplements of games, and popular culture. They frequently have no sense of how people behave outside of the material they consume, hence the construction of the Camarilla which similtaneously portrays them as incredibly shallow and comically evil. They think of the world in terms of superhero comics, with the notion of continuity focused on namechecking parts of the fictional universe, whilst treating death as a temporary inconvenience to popular characters. They write like they have never read a proper book. <br /> <br /> And this is, of course, why we have so many problematic aspects in the modern World of Darkness. They are creating an inherently conservative game, whilst thinking that they are radicals, producing art. They promote dubious, reactionary politics, whilst imagining they are progressives. They have taken what should be a popular intellectual property into the doldrums. <br /> <br /> Now, as I have pointed out before, <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> should be far more successful than it is at present. It's a game set in the contemporary world, with sexy bloodsuckers, and the potential to capitalise upon modern political concerns and the power of vampires in modern popular culture. That it isn't more of a success suggests that somewhere, something has gone badly wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:58:23-07:00","id":1487157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487140#post1487140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most of human history and arguably now, there's no need to explain WHY the upper class are the upper class. They are because they are and the system exists to protect THEM not you. The Camarilla is slightly better than historical feudalism, though, because it DOES provide the stability of the Masquerade and covering up for idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not really true. There was a huge amount of writing throughout history to try to explain how societies function as they do, and why there is an upper class, from the fierce debates over the notion of estates in medieval and early modern Europe, to the frameworks around varna and jati in India. Even today, the notion of what constitutes an upper class and how it functions is a more complex question than many people are prepared to admit. <br /> <br /> Also, I know you frequently misuse the example of feudalism, but the point of feudo-vassilic relations was to guarantee the rights of all participants in the system. You have more rights, in a sense, as a medieval peasant than you do as a random neonate, which is kind of an important point. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T03:59:31-07:00","id":1487158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487153#post1487153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that many Anarchs are against Praxis.<br /> <br /> The question of what an Anarch is rebelling against can vary wildly with, &quot;The fact I am not in charge&quot; being a perfectly valid answer.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Against is a strong word, id simply state they don't have praxis. I should probably elaborate I'm talking about praxis in the socio philosophical not in the vtm version.<br /> <br /> Its a legitimate motivation granted, just not a very interesting one. Meaningful conflict is the soul of drama afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-20-2022, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:03:52-07:00","id":1487159,"title":"","content":"My complaints about V5 can basically be summarized as the following if anyone cares:<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat's handling is atrocious. They're the third player character faction.<br /> <br /> * The lack of continuity between how we got from V20 (or Revised) to V5. I am a huge lore junkie and the rich history of V:TM is barely acknowledged outside of Loresheets.<br /> <br /> * The focus on IC content versus OOC content. Both the Camarilla and Anarch books are very bad at explaining what the two sects are all about.<br /> <br /> * The fact the main book didn't have all thirteen clans.<br /> <br /> * Resonance from drinking blood is silly. There, I said it. It's not even hated like the Touchstone system, so much as no one uses it.<br /> <br /> * The Touchstone system is inferior to the one from Requiem.<br /> <br /> * The poor handling of the Signature Characters, particularly the possible killing of Lucita for no good reasonTM.<br /> <br /> * Feeding style takes up way more room in the Corebook than it should and should have been saved for a latter supplement.<br /> <br /> * Speaking of which. The lack of a Player's Guide, which should have been one of the first things produced.<br /> <br /> * Compulsions are a weird restriction to put onto vampires in addition to their Curse. It interferes with roleplay.<br /> <br /> * The books are getting smaller and much more expensive. The Black Hand and Second Inquisition books should be twice or even three times their size.<br /> <br /> * The Beckoning and Gehenna War were thrown in and never really explained. It's a weird thing to introduce a mystery then never solve it.<br /> <br /> * Not a fan of the Lasombra Weakness.<br /> <br /> * OPP really is the only person attempting to make sense of the world-building. If not for Chicago by Night, I'd have no idea how cities functioned in the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487157#post1487157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's not really true. There was a huge amount of writing throughout history to try to explain how societies function as they do, and why there is an upper class, from the fierce debates over the notion of estates in medieval and early modern Europe, to the frameworks around varna and jati in India. Even today, the notion of what constitutes an upper class and how it functions is a more complex question than many people are prepared to admit.<br /> <br /> Also, I know you frequently misuse the example of feudalism, but the point of feudo-vassilic relations was to guarantee the rights of all participants in the system. You have more rights, in a sense, as a medieval peasant than you do as a random neonate, which is kind of an important point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, even then we're getting into the level of what qualifies as a peasant in the Medieval World versus the fledgling thing as well as the rights and guarantees of a vampire in the various Editions. After all, serfdom is a very different condition from a free peasant (but not quite slavery) and slavery itself actually did exist until the 13th century before its revival. Then there's merchants, priests, and other layers of society entirely outside the aristocracy.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting things about 1st Edition V:TM society was there was a fairly decent argument that the entirety of the Anarch cause was asinine because while Kindred were subject to the law of the Prince, they actually had incredible freedom except for the Traditions. It was never really established what the hell the anarchs were rebelling against until later in the series.<br /> <br /> Mark Rein Hagen at least had Lodin and Modius be complete assholes to justify it. In, say, San Fransisco, being an Anarch strikes me as silly because Vannevar Thomas (the original version) just insisted you not be a fuck up about covering up your murders.<br /> <br /> If you didn't heavily force domain and weren't interested in procreation, what exactly did your Anarch have to be so pissed about? They were cyberpunks without the social economic elements of late stage capitalism and transhumanism to define themselves. Revised corrected this by creating Scourges, much more social stratification, and the Camarilla drafting Anarchs as cannon fodder against the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So kudos to Justin Achilli at least bothering to explain what Anarchs had greviances over--even if it was when the Anarchs were on the way out.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Oh and thank you for participating! So glad you're here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-20-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:08:18-07:00","id":1487160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like that kind of runs head long into the fact I am an Anarch fan who loves the Sabbat and hate what happened to them. In fact, one of my major confusions with the fandom is why it's &quot;Anarchs vs. Sabbat&quot; given that there's absolutely so much in common between the two that people are trying to suggest that benefiing one hurts the other. </div> </div> </div>Given your own posts on feeling that the Sabbat took prominence, themes and imagery and even the war with the Camarilla the Anarchs &quot;should&quot; have had, this doesn't feel like it should be that confusing.<br /> <br /> You yourself seem to feel the Anarchs have never had a full coherent identity, in your own direct words just now. If this is in fact true, why would fans of the Sabbat, a group given a full, coherent identity, like the idea that you keep saying things like they're &quot;a branch&quot; of the Anarchs? The game proclaimed that the Anarchs are their own things, and the Sabbat transformed into something else. Why is it confusing that people who were fans of that took the game at its word?<br /> <br /> When you call a sect a branch of another sect, when you make a big ol post saying that sect is nothing without them, you're not saying things share commonalities, you're saying, near literally, one is an inferior sub growth of the other. If you can't acknowledge that the Sabbat evolved into its own thing and instead have to say &quot;The Sabbat are just Anarchs&quot;, you're saying there was no validity or originality to the way in which the Sabbat further evolved. To the point of saying that the Anarchs should have done all the things they did. If you say something is &quot;just&quot; something else, you are saying it has no distinction of its own.<br /> <br /> That's just how that works.<br /> <br /> When the Sabbat in canon say &quot;we're the original Anarchs!&quot;, for those that even bother to still do so, they don't mean it as &quot;we have so much in common&quot;, they mean it as &quot;we have nothing in common with the group now calling themselves the Anarchs save for superficial comparisons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Plenty of fans of the Sabbat clearly see things on those same terms.<br /> <br /> You can argue they are wrong to do so, but it should be pretty clear why it would be bothersome for them when you do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've mentioned this elsewhere but they basically are setting it up as the Dark Ages in the Modern Times. The Anarchs are becoming more spiritual, more violent, more vicious, and more transhumanist in their nature. Which is a sign that the Anarchs are becoming the Sabbat 2.0. This while the Sabbat is becoming a shallow parody of itself. The Camarilla is also treating the Second Inquisition like the Elders treated the First Inquisition, resulting in people flooding to the Anarchs/New Sabbat. It's supposed to be clever, I think. </div> </div> </div>Lots of things are supposed to be clever that in execution instead feel inane and ill thought out. George Lucas liked to keep saying how Star Wars is a &quot;rhyming circle&quot;, which resulted in miles long stretches of dumb things (I know we're all supposed to like the prequels now because of how the sequels were received, but topically to vampire, enough time passing so that you get nostalgia goggles for something that now came out long ago, doesn't mean it was good. There's a reason that Kenobi's &quot;flashbacks&quot; to the prequels and doing a full out &quot;previously on&quot; to them was basically a sizzle reel and not reminding us about how Anakin hates sand and how Padme decided it was a good idea to marry someone that just said he killed a bunch of children).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's underscoring the sects relationship that is central the origins of the Sabbat as well as the canon history of the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat as a whole. </div> </div> </div>In practice, it's saying that a sect with multiple books to its name exploring the depths of its nature and worldview should just be regarded as a sub-branch of another sect. There's no real getting away from that. If you can't see how people who liked those books would take issue with that, I'm not sure what else can be said to you on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what I'm missing. I hate what was done to the Sabbat and think that it is has made the setting much-much worse as a result. </div> </div> </div>And yet, this is you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>If you remove the Anarch philosophy from the Sabbat, they have nothing.</i> </div> </div> </div>And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>They're a particularly extreme sect of them but let's not pretend they're anything more than an extreme and effective sect of them. They exist to overthrow the Elders, the Antediluvians especially, and engage in all the same violent revolutionary rhetoric as well as terrorism as the Anarchs because they are Anarchs.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They will never be anything more because their identity is Anarchs in total war as well as rejecting Humanity.</i> </div> </div> </div>And outright saying this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The entire metaplot of the game is about the conflict between the Anarchs and Camarilla.</i> </div> </div> </div>All of these things require as their logical premise, for the Sabbat to have no validity in its own right. The game itself treated these groups as three distinct sects in various points of its publication history. For people that preferred that, this is the equivalent of you saying &quot;well I'm ignoring everything that doesn't agree with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do I have the reputation as the V5 promoter here so much that people assume I just defend everything?<br /> <br /> Serious question. </div> </div> </div>If this is a question people are actually allowed to answer, it is in part because you do things like phrase what you think &quot;V5 did wrong&quot; in ways that somehow still note it was correct overall to have done it. You want to say that you think the Sabbat were not handled well in V5, but then you at the exact same time say the Sabbat never existed in their own right as a sect anyway, despite even little things like multiple books with the word &quot;Sabbat&quot; on them. They don't even get their own name, that they chose, for themselves.<br /> <br /> You want to say the Sabbat were handled wrong, but going by what you seem to want for vampire, they would have never existed as anything other than an Anarch fringe group in the first place, and you've now spent multiple posts calling them an Anarch fringe group and defending that.<br /> <br /> And cripes it is weird to be the one pointing this stuff out, when the Sabbat are like.. my #3 favorite sect, behind, if I ponder it, the Camarilla at 2, and Autarkis at 1 (yes, I know, being Autarkis isn't actually a sect :P)<br /> <br /> That said, if I get to include Dark Ages Sects, completely different rankings.<br /> <br /> Though really I found all the sects playable except for the True Black Hand, and eventually I got over myself that it is fine that people like the True Black Hand even though I don't.<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> The issue, certainly for some, again if you really mean this seriously: You talk about how you feel X, Y or Z in V5 was not great, but somehow the game still in the end seems to match pretty accurately what you will then at the same time say Vampire should be like.<br /> <br /> And anything more than that in answering that question would probably go too deep frankly, but if I had to sum it up, it feels like for you, V5 is only allowed to be wrong in the ways you say it is wrong, and any other issue said outside of those reflects a lacking understanding of history, morality, geopolitics, gaming, or just vampire itself. So it has the results it has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm saying that I love the Anarchs and the reason that I love the Sabbat is in large part because that I love the stuff in the Sabbat that is in the Anarchs, which is most of their philosophy only taken to the extreme. I don't believe this is logically inconsistent. Mind you, if you don't think the Anarchs and Sabbat are remotely similar then I can see how this argument would not persuade you. </div> </div> </div>Again, saying that you love the Sabbat as an extension of a group they no longer even use as their primary name, is going to read how it reads. Especially when you throw in &quot;so canonically the Sabbat made a huge effort post the Anarch revolt to develop an entire transhumanist thing to reframe themselves, but they're really just Anarch philosophy taken to an extreme.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is only logically consistent if you view the Sabbat as having no valid identity of their own, nor having evolved in a way that makes them markedly distinct from their origins. Which you seemingly don't. And for people that do, this reads thereby as deeply dismissive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:14:36-07:00","id":1487161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487155#post1487155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think there is something inherently interesting in who is writing the game now, how they view the world, and the ultimate consequence for the nature of the game. Back when <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> was first published, the writers at the time where trying to do something different from the game landscape of the era. Their frame of reference was literature and academia, the monsters were metaphorical, and the challenges faced by the players revolved around characters and interpersonal drama. There is a reason why a number of the characters in the first edition of <i>Chicago by Night</i> were derived from characters in <i>The Jungle</i>, and one gets the sense that the author hadn't merely read the book for the purposes of research.<br /> <br /> Of course, it didn't always work, but this was something fresh and different, and fascinating to anyone who had started out with mainstream games. Those of us who were young at the time played these games, became invested in the universe, and made the World of Darkness into one of the great sales success it was during the 1990s.<br /> <br /> And then we grew up.<br /> <br /> In my case, I worked, completed a PhD, and ended up working for a very large commercial organisation. I read actual literary works, and write material for my employer which is more widely consumed than the average V5 supplement. I do write <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> supplements for the Storyteller's Vault in my spare time, as it is a break from the super-serious work I actually do for proper money. I see the flaws of the old White Wolf books more readily than I did when they were first published, but also see the intellectual and creative potential. Which is why I sometimes post on this forum.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I feel that the people who take the professional lead in the game have taken a very different path. They have been very immersed in the gaming scene for decades; their frame of reference for the world are the supplements of games, and popular culture. They frequently have no sense of how people behave outside of the material they consume, hence the construction of the Camarilla which similtaneously portrays them as incredibly shallow and comically evil. They think of the world in terms of superhero comics, with the notion of continuity focused on namechecking parts of the fictional universe, whilst treating death as a temporary inconvenience to popular characters. They write like they have never read a proper book.<br /> <br /> And this is, of course, why we have so many problematic aspects in the modern World of Darkness. They are creating an inherently conservative game, whilst thinking that they are radicals, producing art. They promote dubious, reactionary politics, whilst imagining they are progressives. They have taken what should be a popular intellectual property into the doldrums.<br /> <br /> Now, as I have pointed out before, <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> should be far more successful than it is at present. It's a game set in the contemporary world, with sexy bloodsuckers, and the potential to capitalise upon modern political concerns and the power of vampires in modern popular culture. That it isn't more of a success suggests that somewhere, something has gone badly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh damn! I've bought some of your stuff! I have nothing intelligent or of value to note here, that's just neat!<br /> <br /> (I might have something of value to say later, this is just neat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:18:42-07:00","id":1487163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487150#post1487150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI - Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> for discussing the subject with me in depth, I'm having a lot of fun and hope you are too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not in some dire mood about it if that's a concern. This forum very solidly gives me a quasi-constructive thing to engage in while waiting for things like medications to kick in and etc.<br /> <br /> Would I prefer there was different phrasing sometimes?<br /> <br /> Sure.<br /> <br /> But I regardless appreciate you noting that the conversations have had value to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:19:24-07:00","id":1487164,"title":"","content":"Thank you for explaining, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a>, I appreciate you taking the time to lay out your reasoning and understand your position.<br /> <br /> Yes, it does seem like I'm crapping on the Sabbat and apologize.<br /> <br /> I do think of the Sabbat as a Anarch offshoot but think of them as &quot;Anarchs but more extreme&quot; is a compliment not a insult. Certainly, it was meant to be a request people see they have more in common than without and fans of one should like the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue, certainly for some, again if you really mean this seriously: You talk about how you feel X, Y or Z in V5 was not great, but somehow the game still in the end seems to match pretty accurately what you will then at the same time say Vampire should be like. </div> </div> </div>Gotcha.<br /> <br /> Well, I listed some complaints above that hopefully provide some context but if I were to change anything, I'd say the Sabbat's handling was mostly bad and I don't really have any real defense for it and think there's no justifying no playable Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, I would support a degenerating Sabbat but only in the context of a game to try to stop it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:19:26-07:00","id":1487165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487159#post1487159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My complaints about V5 can basically be summarized as the following if anyone cares:<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> * The focus on IC content versus OOC content. Both the Camarilla and Anarch books are very bad at explaining what the two sects are all about.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, one quite noticeable detail of the first and second editions of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is that in-character text was used incredibly sparingly. It does appear in places, but only as one of a variety of writing techniques. In-character text generally has a poor information-to-word-count ratio, and has become significantly overused as a technique, mostly serving as literary wallpaper. Were I developing the game, this is something I would completely ban contributors from writing in-character...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:21:15-07:00","id":1487166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487165#post1487165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, one quite noticeable detail of the first and second editions of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is that in-character text was used incredibly sparingly. It does appear in places, but only as one of a variety of writing techniques. In-character text generally has a poor information-to-word-count ratio, and has become significantly overused as a technique, mostly serving as literary wallpaper. Were I developing the game, this is something I would completely ban contributors from writing in-character...</div> </div> </div> </div>Random aside but I feel like it first became a problem with HUNTER: THE RECKONING.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:58:15-07:00","id":1487171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487155#post1487155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think there is something inherently interesting in who is writing the game now, how they view the world, and the ultimate consequence for the nature of the game. Back when <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> was first published, the writers at the time where trying to do something different from the game landscape of the era. Their frame of reference was literature and academia, the monsters were metaphorical, and the challenges faced by the players revolved around characters and interpersonal drama. There is a reason why a number of the characters in the first edition of <i>Chicago by Night</i> were derived from characters in <i>The Jungle</i>, and one gets the sense that the author hadn't merely read the book for the purposes of research.<br /> <br /> Of course, it didn't always work, but this was something fresh and different, and fascinating to anyone who had started out with mainstream games. Those of us who were young at the time played these games, became invested in the universe, and made the World of Darkness into one of the great sales success it was during the 1990s.<br /> <br /> And then we grew up.<br /> <br /> In my case, I worked, completed a PhD, and ended up working for a very large commercial organisation. I read actual literary works, and write material for my employer which is more widely consumed than the average V5 supplement. I do write <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> supplements for the Storyteller's Vault in my spare time, as it is a break from the super-serious work I actually do for proper money. I see the flaws of the old White Wolf books more readily than I did when they were first published, but also see the intellectual and creative potential. Which is why I sometimes post on this forum.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I feel that the people who take the professional lead in the game have taken a very different path. They have been very immersed in the gaming scene for decades; their frame of reference for the world are the supplements of games, and popular culture. They frequently have no sense of how people behave outside of the material they consume, hence the construction of the Camarilla which similtaneously portrays them as incredibly shallow and comically evil. They think of the world in terms of superhero comics, with the notion of continuity focused on namechecking parts of the fictional universe, whilst treating death as a temporary inconvenience to popular characters. They write like they have never read a proper book.<br /> <br /> And this is, of course, why we have so many problematic aspects in the modern World of Darkness. They are creating an inherently conservative game, whilst thinking that they are radicals, producing art. They promote dubious, reactionary politics, whilst imagining they are progressives. They have taken what should be a popular intellectual property into the doldrums.<br /> <br /> Now, as I have pointed out before, <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> should be far more successful than it is at present. It's a game set in the contemporary world, with sexy bloodsuckers, and the potential to capitalise upon modern political concerns and the power of vampires in modern popular culture. That it isn't more of a success suggests that somewhere, something has gone badly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let me try and say something vaguely more intelligent here.<br /> <br /> For context: So, without getting into too much detail, I am someone who deeply depends on a social safety net provided by a wide scale organized society existing, certainly as far as healthcare and disability, in order for me to continue existing. And wah hoo hah it is tough being disabled several times over and having pretty lefty politics in The Left, not just because of how if you dig deeply enough, oh there you are eugenics. (The right and the center of course also love eugenics if you dig deeply enough. Woeful state of affairs.)<br /> <br /> Again, I am only saying this for context. I feel like I need to flash that as a warning disclaimer.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the one impact I would say that sort of life experience has had on me is to deeply weary me of narratives like the ones in HtR 5th, or the ones the V5 have. Or simply the one Mage the Ascension rolled with for so long.<br /> <br /> I bounce pretty hard these days off the &quot;the only real good can be found in scrappy bands of individuals! higher organizing is inherently flawed at best!&quot; routine, because I bounce pretty hard off of it in life.<br /> <br /> (I apparently need to say it, but it doesn't mean I think fictional evil groups in the fictional WoD are good actually, it means I'm just so very tired of what the presented counter narrative to them is)<br /> <br /> I mean, to really look at it, I sometimes want to scream &quot;you know you guys are just preaching a particular flavour of libertarianism and calling yourselves progressive?&quot;, yes.<br /> <br /> That *completely* aside, I think that certainly there's something so odd about a game that has basically become about itself, at the same time wanting to say it is bad/wrong to refer to itself, and yet at the same time explicitly being an attempt to define itself largely by its own material from coming up on three decades ago. There is honestly nothing theoretically wrong with VtM being about VtM, at least in a business sense. DnD stopped being about fantasy in a broader sense ages ago, as opposed to being about itself, and it makes a mint.<br /> <br /> You could argue that DnD is helped by that the latest edition offers a comparatively sizable chunk of room for being about itself, but there's also a case to be made for the impact of the rise of the actual play industry, virtual tabletops, what all have you.<br /> <br /> That VtM seems to only be capitalizing on all such stuff in a more minor way is notable, I agree. Like I say, we're four years in, the ttrpg would not still be published if it wasn't selling to some satisfying degree, but I think the idea of VtM, at least as a table top roleplaying game, ever being big as it was is lost and gone away. It's a little sad, because there have been some absolute waves of vampire stuff popularity it just hasn't managed to hook into (or, when it was the only game in town by contrast, that VtR didn't manage to hook into).<br /> <br /> Still, VtM ages ago stopped being about anything besides itself if you even remotely had an awareness of any popular media vampire trends, at any time in the last decade and change. And V5 doubles down on that, just with an extra helping of &quot;but now only about VtM in this really specific way&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I've said before, it's like a strange OSR-esque situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-20-2022, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T05:06:30-07:00","id":1487174,"title":"","content":"Except HtR did it to actual good and purposeful effect. The muddled messages communicated by all of the in-character passages HtR uses helps to emphasize how little the Imbued really know, and are all largely operating on partial truths. The H-net framework also made sure it was much more delineated between in-character sections and third person narration from the book authors to state the &quot;truth&quot; of the setting/lore.<br /> <br /> It was bad from very early on. You can look at the first WtA Tribebooks where you see who sections of books are technically being written from an in-character perspective; even when that's all the coverage many topics get when they need a third person narrator to get into depth that an in-character presenter can't. This is something that's plague the WoD games from pretty much the get go, as lots and lots of &quot;facts&quot; of the setting are technically only presented from an in-character biased and individual perspective; but the readers are left to assume that perspective is accurate because nothing expands or contradicts it.<br /> <br /> Banned in-character presenters feels like it dulls the character and color of the text to me, but RPG books do much better when it's clearly separated and the third person narrator sections actually get the space they need.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Though... something something.... Bloodhunt? I'm really lost as to where how to try to hook any of this back to the thread's topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T05:08:12-07:00","id":1487176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487174#post1487174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except HtR did it to actual good and purposeful effect. The muddled messages communicated by all of the in-character passages HtR uses helps to emphasize how little the Imbued really know, and are all largely operating on partial truths. The H-net framework also made sure it was much more delineated between in-character sections and third person narration from the book authors to state the &quot;truth&quot; of the setting/lore.<br /> <br /> It was bad from very early on. You can look at the first WtA Tribebooks where you see who sections of books are technically being written from an in-character perspective; even when that's all the coverage many topics get when they need a third person narrator to get into depth that an in-character presenter can't. This is something that's plague the WoD games from pretty much the get go, as lots and lots of &quot;facts&quot; of the setting are technically only presented from an in-character biased and individual perspective; but the readers are left to assume that perspective is accurate because nothing expands or contradicts it.<br /> <br /> Banned in-character presenters feels like it dulls the character and color of the text to me, but RPG books do much better when it's clearly separated and the third person narrator sections actually get the space they need.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Though... something something.... Bloodhunt? I'm really lost as to where how to try to hook any of this back to the thread's topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My last attempt to be topical was just noting that it's pretty wild how different Bloodhunt and the V5 tabletop game are, if that helps you out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T10:33:48-07:00","id":1487206,"title":"","content":"I played Bloodhunt at launch. I did not like it. If this is the most &quot;successful&quot; VTM game, then the VTM gaming sphere is doomed. My opinion over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T10:47:54-07:00","id":1487207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487206#post1487206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played Bloodhunt at launch. I did not like it. If this is the most &quot;successful&quot; VTM game, then the VTM gaming sphere is doomed. My opinion over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here, I tried playing it for a bit, and then tried again last week, but it's really not a VtM game, it's 'Fortnite with Fangs', and it's so reliant on twitch features that only those with excellent skills can be anything other than victims in the game.<br /> <br /> While they've scraped up some lore and kind of used the clans as inspiration for the 'classes' in the game, and the map and traversing it is interesting, it's 90% about guns, which just ends up being tedious. The developers aren't interested in listening to anyone who makes any suggestions or thoughts to the contrary of their chosen direction, and, in the long run, I'm pretty sure it's not going to do well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T11:09:19-07:00","id":1487210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487206#post1487206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played Bloodhunt at launch. I did not like it. If this is the most &quot;successful&quot; VTM game, then the VTM gaming sphere is doomed. My opinion over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the success of one money making spin off precludes the success of other variants. Indeed, the visual novels and other variety of gaming only benefits the IP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487207#post1487207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same here, I tried playing it for a bit, and then tried again last week, but it's really not a VtM game, it's 'Fortnite with Fangs', and it's so reliant on twitch features that only those with excellent skills can be anything other than victims in the game.<br /> <br /> While they've scraped up some lore and kind of used the clans as inspiration for the 'classes' in the game, and the map and traversing it is interesting, it's 90% about guns, which just ends up being tedious. The developers aren't interested in listening to anyone who makes any suggestions or thoughts to the contrary of their chosen direction, and, in the long run, I'm pretty sure it's not going to do well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the developers are adding more roleplay elements but it will never be an RPG.<br /> <br /> Nor is it a substitute for Bloodlines 2, which is being held under lock and key for the past year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:33:08-07:00","id":1487230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487210#post1487210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the success of one money making spin off precludes the success of other variants. Indeed, the visual novels and other variety of gaming only benefits the IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>A common trend for video game companies/developers is to try to stick to what is the most popular model they've produce. If an executive with shares in the IP sees Bloodhunt as successful, regardless of if it is or not, then they may demand more resources go into it. I personally did not enjoy the game, and hope that this does not cause issues.<br /> <br /> Game development is a chain of production, so there's a good chance I'm overreacting. On the slim chance that this does happen, I will be disappointed basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T13:14:06-07:00","id":1487241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487210#post1487210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the success of one money making spin off precludes the success of other variants. Indeed, the visual novels and other variety of gaming only benefits the IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it isn't so black and white.<br /> <br /> A horizontal first (getting the IP out is as many kinds of formats as possible) transmedia approach can end up bad for the IP compared to a vertical first (investing in a small number of formats first) one.<br /> <br /> The horizontal approach works... if it works. It's something of a high-risk high reward strategy. When it works, it shows that the IP works in all sorts of media, and thus has value to a wide range of licensees. But it can easily backfire if the only positive results are limited to a small number of projects. If you go wide, but only interactive fiction gets positive reviews will action videogames tank, and so on, you get pigeonholed as only being valuable as a brand to IF related products.<br /> <br /> The vertical approach is more conservative: build up the brand around products it already has a positive track record of. It's slower to get up to media juggernaut status, but it lets you focus resources and play to the IP's core strengths. Then you leverage that success to branch out horizontally slowly (over saturation is a risk here).<br /> <br /> Paradox seems to have miscalculated. They seem to presume they were doing a vertical approach and are now branching out using the oWW and Onyx Path efforts as the vertical core building of the brand. However, they're really doing a wide horizontal approach because the WoD brand had faded too much under CCP's ownership. As such, things like Bloodlines 2 being delayed this long, and Bloodhunt on the verge of tanking hurt the brand far more than some success elsewhere. It's not that success in other styles of play is bad for the IP directly, but it goes back to the issue of devaluing the brand as only being good for certain types of games and harming the potential to leverage the IP in other avenues later down the line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:51:32-07:00","id":1487267,"title":"","content":"I think a larger issue was the degredation of the World of Darkness IP in the public consciousness as a whole is something to be concerned about. While there's plenty of die-hard fans who continued to love it from the Nineties to today without any real break in that fandom, the simple fact was that it had completely fallen off of the radar.<br /> <br /> So yes, I have been taking Blood Hunt as a positive just because the more noise made about VAMPIRES ARE ALIVE, the better for the IP as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0ydRhwnwk-s\" data-code=\"0ydRhwnwk-s\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0ydRhwnwk-s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:36:18-07:00","id":1487296,"title":"","content":"That is, however, why I brought up what I did. Bloodhunt needs to turn around, and turn around fast, or the message is not &quot;Vampires are Alive!&quot; but, &quot;Paradox is trying to zap vampires back to life even though you can't defib a dead heart.&quot; Every piece of bad PR is far stronger in public perception than good PR, and continues to push the perception that Paradox can't make the WoD a huge brand again.<br /> <br /> Even if Bloodlines 2 comes out, every quarter it gets delay, the bar it needs to hit on release goes up. There's a whole body of works that fans clamored for, for years, but were disappointed not because the final product was bad per se, but because it wasn't worth the wait. Chinese Democracy probably would have been a hit record if it was only a year late, but 15 years later and GnR fans had moved on. Duke Nukem Forever suffered the same fate: if it had happened closer to the original it could have been a huge game. Coming out so much later after fans had written it off, it needed to not just be a decent game, it needed to be a masterpiece to get fans back.<br /> <br /> If we get BL 2 in 2025? It could be a solid game and still damage the brand in the long term because it should have been out already and people aren't going to care for a decent BL 2 that many years late. BL 2 is going to need to be an amazing game now.<br /> <br /> The degradation of the brand should have been a concern for nWW/Paradox's plans five years ago, not something being figured out now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:54:08-07:00","id":1487298,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my perspective versus <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> is that the brand is definitely FAR more prevalent than it was before V5 and they've managed to really insert it back into the public consciousness with Blood Hunt and the Live Plays.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Paradox has definitely pulled it from nonexistence into awareness and keeps going forward but its still far from where it could be.<br /> <br /> But I know we disagree on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:01:26-07:00","id":1487325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487298#post1487298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, my perspective versus <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> is that the brand is definitely FAR more prevalent than it was before V5 and they've managed to really insert it back into the public consciousness with Blood Hunt and the Live Plays.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Paradox has definitely pulled it from nonexistence into awareness and keeps going forward but its still far from where it could be.<br /> <br /> But I know we disagree on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure how, after this whole thread, you see Bloodhunt as a success. The Live Plays got a nice buzz when they started, but the later episodes dropped sharply to the point that the average on those is around 150k viewers. That's not a blistering success. The last episode of that was well over 2 years ago. And I'm not sure how well New York by Night will do, but right now it's at 120k views for the hyped first episode.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:15:52-07:00","id":1487329,"title":"","content":"This is basically part of a pattern. There's clearly interest in the WoD IP beyond the hardcore TTRPG fans. Bloodlines 2 was massively hyped all over because of Bloodlines 1's cult status. LA by Night peaked at ~1 million views IIRC. Bloodhunt had a great launch. Even V5 started pretty strong.<br /> <br /> But, at varying paces, this doesn't last. The live plays core audience is big, but not spectacular. The longer BL 2 stays in development the more it harms the profitability of the final product. Bloodhunt's numbers crashed, and as the other thread as covered fans are souring significantly because of the opacity and delays. V5 supplements aren't getting the attention the core book did.<br /> <br /> Whatever that kernel of love for the IP is in the wider audience, Paradox isn't finding a way to tap into it. The nostalgia factor gets a lot of eyes, but it seems like it's a constant series of failures when it comes from turning eyes and hype into repeat customers. <br /> <br /> Either the WoD isn't really capable of being made widely relevant to modern audiences, or there's something deep rooted in 5th that's undermining the efforts to make it so. If WoD can be made mainstream again, something needs to change because... the high point of V5 being Bloodhunt's May player numbers would be a disaster for the brand that would taint it in the public eye; possibly for good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:16:09-07:00","id":1487330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487325#post1487325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still not sure how, after this whole thread, you see Bloodhunt as a success. The Live Plays got a nice buzz when they started, but the later episodes dropped sharply to the point that the average on those is around 150k viewers. That's not a blistering success. The last episode of that was well over 2 years ago. And I'm not sure how well New York by Night will do, but right now it's at 120k views for the hyped first episode.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the thread was inspired by the articles that were talking about its big success and Outstars recent video on its expansion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZW1eM-ZGD4Y\" data-code=\"ZW1eM-ZGD4Y\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZW1eM-ZGD4Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:29:36-07:00","id":1487332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487230#post1487230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an executive with shares in the IP sees Bloodhunt as successful, regardless of if it is or not, then they may demand more resources go into it. I personally did not enjoy the game, and hope that this does not cause issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the business model here. Paradox has no part on Bloodhunt, it's from a licensee.<br /> <br /> No matter what happens to it, there's no such a thing as someone in Paradox investing too much in it. The problem here really is just the effect it will have on other potential licensees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487330#post1487330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the thread was inspired by the articles that were talking about its big success and Outstars recent video on its expansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've been repeatedly told that a good start doesn't means much for the model of game Bloodhunt is.<br /> <br /> It is an ongoing service. It needs a good first <b>year</b>. The articles related a good first <b>month</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:56:36-07:00","id":1487337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487332#post1487332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an ongoing service. It needs a good first <b>year</b>. The articles related a good first <b>month</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I mentioned earlier my point is about the reception of the game compared to the other IP video game releases. In which Blood Hunt has massively overshadowed them.<br /> <br /> It's not something I'm happy about because Blood Hunt is not the kind of game I'd like to be the flagship of the IP for.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm aware the game isn't performing great. Its just the best versus all the other ones. It's not in the top ten Battle Royal games.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/AyEfWEx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-21-2022, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T03:47:59-07:00","id":1487346,"title":"","content":"It's not a flagship product if it tanks.<br /> <br /> Also, define &quot;best&quot; here in a meaningful fashion. You seem to be treating &quot;most downloads&quot; as best. But why is that best? Bigger is not always better.<br /> <br /> To go back to an old example of mine: It's better to make a movie for $10 million that sells $50 million worth of tickets, than make a movie for $200 million, that sells $150 million worth of tickets. Not only is the first one a better option financially, it's a better impression on audiences. Blumhouse is an insanely good brand for horror fans. For everyone else? Maybe not. But they know how to make good genre films cheap, which means lots of profit and goodwill. Their bad horror movies frequently do better than what much bigger studios do with the genre. <br /> <br /> You don't need to have a &quot;flagship&quot; game. If you can regularly do games that are really popular among a niche market, you can build a brand of making good games without getting pigeonholed: it just takes knowing how to be the &quot;we find quality people to make games set in our universe and then let them make awesome games.&quot; Something Paradox doesn't seem to have figured out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T03:50:22-07:00","id":1487348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487346#post1487346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a flagship product if it tanks.<br /> <br /> Also, define &quot;best&quot; here in a meaningful fashion. You seem to be treating &quot;most downloads&quot; as best. But why is that best? Bigger is not always better.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I'm trying to discuss what the majority of people are playing outside of tabletop RPGers.<br /> <br /> Blood Hunt is the thing that has the most market penetration over the other New WoD products I've listed.<br /> <br /> Or do you disagree?<br /> <br /> If you feel like there's a much better example, please tell me. I'd like to be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:07:46-07:00","id":1487350,"title":"","content":"How do you do a fair comparison of market penetration between different service types? As we keep saying, Bloodhunt is a service that's only been around for three months. It's a product that can only be analyzed in much longer time frames to be meaningful.<br /> <br /> You're trying to compare how many people went and saw <i>Nope</i> in theatres so far, with how Shudder's subscription numbers are doing. Where are we even supposed to try to say which is doing &quot;better&quot; or what market penetration looks like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:18:10-07:00","id":1487353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487350#post1487350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you do a fair comparison of market penetration between different service types? As we keep saying, Bloodhunt is a service that's only been around for three months. It's a product that can only be analyzed in much longer time frames to be meaningful.<br /> <br /> You're trying to compare how many people went and saw <i>Nope</i> in theatres so far, with how Shudder's subscription numbers are doing. Where are we even supposed to try to say which is doing &quot;better&quot; or what market penetration looks like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm more interested in IP recognition rather than hard sales as that will effect the demand for products in the future like the series.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:43:10-07:00","id":1487357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487353#post1487353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I'm more interested in IP recognition rather than hard sales as that will effect the demand for products in the future like the series.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would like to point out that recognition is not always a good thing, Twilight is pretty damn famous but definitely not in a good way, V5 products so far received enough exposure to break the &quot;niche&quot; denomination they had before (although masquerade has always been much better known than your average indie title) but that is definitely not a mark of success, especially considering the mediocre quality of most of it's spin off products, that is without gettin in the actual books, the less said about them the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:59:18-07:00","id":1487363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487330#post1487330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the thread was inspired by the articles that were talking about its big success and Outstars recent video on its expansion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZW1eM-ZGD4Y\" data-code=\"ZW1eM-ZGD4Y\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZW1eM-ZGD4Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It's Outstar's JOB to be hyped up, happy tell everyone how everything is awesome and how everything is successful and how all us fans are all over the moon with the World of Darkness. Are you going by what the Community Manager has to say or by cold hard facts we can glean from the articles you (among others) linked throughout this thread?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T05:21:42-07:00","id":1487370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487346#post1487346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a flagship product if it tanks.<br /> <br /> Also, define &quot;best&quot; here in a meaningful fashion. You seem to be treating &quot;most downloads&quot; as best. But why is that best? Bigger is not always better.<br /> <br /> To go back to an old example of mine: It's better to make a movie for $10 million that sells $50 million worth of tickets, than make a movie for $200 million, that sells $150 million worth of tickets. Not only is the first one a better option financially, it's a better impression on audiences. Blumhouse is an insanely good brand for horror fans. For everyone else? Maybe not. But they know how to make good genre films cheap, which means lots of profit and goodwill. Their bad horror movies frequently do better than what much bigger studios do with the genre.<br /> <br /> You don't need to have a &quot;flagship&quot; game. If you can regularly do games that are really popular among a niche market, you can build a brand of making good games without getting pigeonholed: it just takes knowing how to be the &quot;we find quality people to make games set in our universe and then let them make awesome games.&quot; Something Paradox doesn't seem to have figured out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very good perspective. A couple of smaller, cheaper cult classics would do more for the brand than large big scale games that take forever. They are easier and more straightforward to make and profit from and their market impact is significantly bigger than the average tabletop RPG. Vampire came back with a huge marketing push and glorious announcements and then didn't have a lot to show for it. We're what... 7 years away from their IP purchase and 4 years away from V5 coming out, and honestly the most succesfull and well accepted products we've had so far were the visual novels.<br /> <br /> Werewolf got a bigger standalone release and an action game, but it's already 50% off after not even 6 months its out, and generally the sales and buzz for it don't seem impressive.<br /> Blood Hunt was a bigger release than Werewolf and a game as service - it's not really hitting its stride right now.<br /> Bloodlines is just vapourware at this point. If they really hired a new team and went back to basics and even if they can salvage the assests and code that was running they're at least 2-3 years away from pushing something out - 9-10 years after their acquistion and 6-7 from V5.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T11:06:51-07:00","id":1487405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487353#post1487353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I'm more interested in IP recognition rather than hard sales as that will effect the demand for products in the future like the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. So good brand recognition, bad brand recognition, neutral recognition, or any recognition?<br /> <br /> BL 2 probably had the best &quot;opening&quot; good brand recognition that's turned to sour bad brand recognition because of the delays. The eyes on from hype when they were in full push mode before the first version of the game was huge. Way more people were following all the publicity and social media stuff than Bloodhunt got players in May. I'm sure way more people are upset about the status of BL 2 than Bloodhunt too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T20:37:25-07:00","id":1487441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486924-bloodhunt-is-apparently-5th-edition-s-biggest-success?p=1487337#post1487337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I mentioned earlier my point is about the reception of the game compared to the other IP video game releases. In which Blood Hunt has massively overshadowed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Bloodhunt tanks, it'll turn 180\u00b0 into bad rep.<br /> <br /> Any good rep is better than bad rep, it's almost as simple as arithmetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}